2026-07-20 22:41:52,263 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48468 (CSTEST-655): summary='Jump Distance' description='As a surgeon, I would want to know the how jump distance changes along the liner circumference to maximize joint stability, especially when planning lipped or anteverted liners.\n\n* A view of the cup opening should be provided, with labels to indicate anterior (A), posterior (P), lateral (L), and medial (M) directions.\n* If a lipped or anteverted liner is selected, a line from the center of the cup to the apex of the lip should be drawn to indicate lip orientation. The liner can be positioned within the cup at 12 discrete positions, which are usually described as 1, 2, … 12 o’clock. A drop-down menu should provide the option to modify lip orientation (i.e., switch between the different “o’clock” positions). \n*  Jump distance is defined as the distance the femoral head needs to travel before dislocating after impingement occurred. It is a purely geometric feature that mostly depends on the height of the liner. When lipped or anteverted liners are used, lip height progressively changes throughout the liner circumference, reaching its peak at the lip apex and at the opposite side of the apex. Therefore jump distance should be depicted by color-coding the liner circumference and with a legend indicating max and min jump distance for the selected liner. \n* The cup opening view where jump distance is depicted should also be used to display more cleanly the implant-on-implant impingement areas. Therefore, similarly to the 3D model in the neutral pose, the cup opening should show a summary of the areas where overlap between implant components occurs during ADL simulations.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,265 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48171 (CSTEST-654): summary='NSYNC: Data Transfer and Database Management' description='Host Dynamic memory for web planner\n\nAPI map\n\nSwagger - type of data exchange between services \n\nRecord of truth is always in NSYNC \n\nNo permanent data in the Planner\n\nGatekeeper between web planner and VCM\n\nICD - Data being exchanged \n\n* Sudarshan (what the data is) \n* Reusing NSYNC and KPOP schemas would be ideal ( patient schema , procedure schema about physicians etc. , surgery schema about the actual procedure etc )  \n* Discussed on 6/16: Image generation and pdf report generation in AWS (Externalized); Discussed on 7/7: image generation and pdf report generation in new VPC on Lumino that will also host surgeon web planner and implant database instance that web planner will access; IDB Hosting also in new VPC\n\n\n\nAll parameters of Planner should be stored in Parameter manager in AWS ( Externalized ) - Configuration management will be shared between VCM and Planner' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,265 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48172 (CSTEST-653): summary='Pre-Op Hip - Cloud Architecture' description='VPC Architecture - Pittsburgh?\n\nVPC content Development - CG? Alythia? Visionaire? \n\nVPC Maintenance - Visionaire? \n\n\n\nNew virtual private cloud (VPC) on Lumino to host: \n\n* Surgeon web planner\n* Implant data base (IDB) (instance that surgeon web planner will access)\n* Kinematic simulation data (instance that surgeon web planner will access)???\n* pdf Report generation (in addition to image generation to produce images needed to populate report)' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
