2026-07-20 22:41:52,294 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48487 (CSTEST-634): summary='PreOp Hip - 2D Workflow' description='Web Planner needs to handle cases without CT information. In general, Web Planner needs to import the case information and when patient specific pelvic and femur bones files, or specific implant size, placement information is not available, Web Planner assumes predefined default values for those cases, and uses generic pelvic model without femur. Impingement analysis doesn’t include bone surface files. Two most common CT-free scenarios are described below. A general message or surgeon \n\n# CT-free scenarios - Two Lateral Xrays\n\n* Web planner imports plan for patient specific information and *uses generic pelvic bone without femur* in the absence of bone model in the plan.\n* Web planner informs user that the Visionaire plan *assumed implant sizes, placements* in the absence of patient CT scan, and *only implant-implant impingement shown*.\n* Use of appropriate color scheme to differentiate between bone-bone & implant-implant  implant impingement implant-implant impingement only .\n\n2. No Images scenario\n\n* Web planner imports plan for patient specific information and *uses generic pelvic bone without femur, generic implants sizes and placements* in the absence of bone model and SPM information in the plan.\n* Another option for steps above could be to just have a predefined demo plan always available for the user to update. This feature could also be treated as *training* tool/feature. Can be completely patient agnostic as well.\n* Web planner informs user that *all implant sizes and placements are assumed, and only implant-implant impingement shown*.\n* Remaining functions same as CT-based case planning.\n\n3. AP Xray -\n\n* Web planner allows *upload* of static AP Xray/ template file (format TBD - examples- .dcm/.pdf/.jpg/.png) from desktop/usb to review.\n\nTBD - Based on risk evaluation determine what can be assumed as a pre-defined values vs what to leave blank/empty and leave it up to the surgeon to select.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
