2026-07-20 22:41:52,309 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48175 (CSTEST-624): summary='Materialise Mimics for CT Segmentation' description='As part of the Hip Pre-operative Planning workflow, once CT images are uploaded and reviewed for quality purposes, they must be processed to produce 3D models of the patient’s bone anatomy; this process is called Segmentation. Several segmentation applications exist on the market. An assessment of these products was conducted to support selection of Materialise Mimics. \n\nSegmentation Vendor Assessment: \n\n[https://smithandnephew-my.sharepoint.com/:x:/g/personal/april_krivoniak_smith-nephew_com/ERNrH23OmD9Lr67npLF1cj4BZ7R_4t13qyUKTQHiphnUAQ?e=xdKlhy|https://smithandnephew-my.sharepoint.com/:x:/g/personal/april_krivoniak_smith-nephew_com/ERNrH23OmD9Lr67npLF1cj4BZ7R_4t13qyUKTQHiphnUAQ?e=xdKlhy|smart-link] \n\nThe Visionaire team is familiar with Materialise Mimics and holds several license seats of the software. The team will update to the latest version of the software to support the hip pre-operative planning workflow. \n\n\n\nLicense Needs: Mimics25 & MedCad' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,311 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48176 (CSTEST-623): summary='VIVS for Hip Imaging QC - PreOp Planning' description='UPDATED 4/28 - Segaway identified as alternative tool which can support image review processes and procedures for hip pre-operative planning. Segaway is an opensource, web-based, medical imaging viewer which supports all imaging modalities, including CT and X-ray (necessary for hip). VIVS does not support CT. See [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-622|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-622|smart-link]. \n\n\n\nAppropriate changes to VIVS software or provide an alternative which can support following - \n\nImport Dicom images CT/Xray\n\nVerify Image quality for parameters like\n\nPatient Name, DOB, Surgical side\n\nScan date\n\nCT protocols - Field of View, Scale, Slice thickness/interval, reconstruction algorithms, disturbance due to movement or metals\n\nXray protocols - Field of view, Scale, disturbance due to movement or metals' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,312 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48177 (CSTEST-622): summary='Segaway for Image Review' description='After upload of patient images to the VCM, the uploaded images are transferred to the patient’s case folder. The images must be reviewed to ensure they meet pre-defined, required specifications and to ensure all necessary images have been uploaded. Erroneous images must be removed from the patient’s case folder. Image review shall occur in a medical image viewer. Segaway is an open-source, web-based, medical imaging viewer used by Visionaire today. Segaway has the ability to view images of any modality. Segaway lacks features tailored Visionaire-specific needs, and these features are necessary to support image review at scale. Segaway also lacks the features which facilitate knee-specific image generation and automated migration of these generated files (VIVS currently supports knee-specific image review processes).' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,312 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48178 (CSTEST-621): summary='VCM UI: User Login, Case Creation, and Case Management' description='The addition of the Hip Pre-operative Planning offering will require a new patient case “Type” to be added in the VCM (Visionaire Customer Management portal), along with subsequent portal updates that capture Hip Pre-operative Planning case information and surgical preference details. Changes will need to propagate to the CRM (customer relationship management) portion of the overarching VCM.\n\nPortal branding considerations needed for the addition of Pre-operative Hip Planning. \n\n\n\nUse Case(s): \n\n* A portal for Surgeon/clinician ordering of pre-operative hip plans.\n* A portal for Surgeon/clinician image upload to support pre-operative hip planning.\n* A portal for Surgeon/clinician review of pre-operative hip plans.\n* A portal for Surgeon/clinician request of updates to pre-operative hip plans.\n* A platform for Visionaire to manage customers of pre-operative hip planning, + their imaging centers.\n* A platform for Visionaire to manage pre-operative hip planning cases throughout the workflow\n\n\n\n* Likely external portal users include: Surgeons, Schedulers, SN Reps, Imaging center technicians\n* Likely internal portal users include: Visionaire Support team members, Visionaire Image Reviewers, Visionaire Segmenters, Visionaire Engineers' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,313 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48494 (CSTEST-620): summary='Data storage, archiving and retrieval solutions' description='' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,314 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48495 (CSTEST-619): summary='Neck cut planning adjustment options' description='As a surgeon, I am able to see the pre-defined neck cut view and neck cut height based on Engineer’s plan of the neck cut once the plan is imported. Similarly, the latest neck cut plan should be reflected in the final plan summary and report. Example image -\n\n!image-20230619-155008.png|width=325,height=217!\n\nInitial neck cut plane (up to 2 planes) could be provided by Engineer’s plan or IDB. \n\nDuring Stem planning (type-size selection and placement), the neck cut plane(s) are also visible. When stem moves, the neck cut plane moves with it. Alternatively, surgeon could move the neck cut plane(s), translate/rotate, independent of the stem position. \n\n3D bone model should reflect the neck cut for rendering display and impingement analysis.\n\nWhen desired, surgeon can view the Neck cut Height (distance between predefined landmarks, i.e. lesser trochanter, and the neck cut plane and bone intersection landmark) otherwise the height value can be hidden during stem planning.\n\n!image-20230511-160401.png|width=518,height=531!\n\nBlue lines in the image below showing two cut planes. Red line showing a single cut plane.\n\n!image-20230619-124857.png|width=8.333333333333332%!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,317 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48496 (CSTEST-618): summary='CT slices integrated with Web Planner for implant planning' description='{color:#ff5630}*Not being considered for initial version*{color}\n\n\n\n\n\nFor user to move implant positions, 3D bone model information alone may be insufficient. In that scenario, user would want additional information to gain confidence in the new implant positions. These additional information could be CT data and hence need to ensure that the Web Planner is capable of viewing CT data.\n\n\n\nOnce the data is imported, *integrated CT* slices to demonstrate implant placement in CT reference frames with corresponding 3D bone model. The CT slice replaces the 2D outline of the 3D bone model in visualization.\n\n\n\nReference - [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-608|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-608|smart-link]\n\n2D Outline of Bone model - (used for Implant placement) Showing the outline of 3D bone model in a specific frame across the depth of 3D bone in respective reference plane (coronal/sagittal/transverse). Example - Using cross hair and 3 different views.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,323 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48497 (CSTEST-617): summary='ADLs2- Impingement Analysis by femur angles' description='* As a surgeon, I would want to know the rotation (Flexion/extension, Abduction/adduction, external/internal rotation) of the femur where initial impingement is detected. \n* When I select a specific activity, I can observe the femur angle values change as the motion for the selected activity of daily living progresses.\n* I can manually move any of the 3 angles. When I change the femur angle values, the 3D bone/implant models move to reflect the changes I enter. \n* My user experience should feel like live interaction and not where I have to wait to see the result. \n\n\n\nExample interaction could look like below.\n\n!image-20230511-161909.png|width=184,height=172!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,326 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48498 (CSTEST-616): summary='Ability to generate pre-op plan report which can be reviewed/referenced outside OR and in the OR' description='Web Planner should be able to generate a plan report on demand. It be commanded to generate an automatic report for the case at a pre-determined stage in the workflow through VCM or user may genera a report when desired. Multiple reports could be generated for the same case, so add date/timestamp/version for tracking.\n\nReport features - Once user validate the plan, either automatically or via dedicated use action Web planner generates report for that plan. \n\n* Web planner needs to generate a report which can be exported to Visionaire .\n* Web planner needs to generate a report which can be viewed on commonly used hardware devices for review, 6” to 70” screen for view only\n* Web planner needs to generate a report which can be printed by commonly used printers\n* Web planner needs to generate a report which can be viewed in Hip 7 viewer via USB import (DICOM compatible file, i.e., .dcm)\n\nPrint compatible report content should include information for - \n\n* Planned surgical outcome parameters\n* Pre-planned parameters\n* Details of Acetabulum Cup planning\n* Details of Femur stem planning\n* Details of Spinopelvic classification\n* Details of neck cut planning\n* Hide PHI data\n\nHip 7 compatible report may be tailored to view on CORI intraoperately. \n\nThe report should be compatible to be printed on a regular 8.5 X 11 inch printer paper. \n\nThe report should be compatible to be viewed on different screens from 6” to 70”.\n\n\n\n{color:#bf2600}Action: PDF encryption needed or not.{color}' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,326 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48499 (CSTEST-615): summary='Delete - Identification of implant and bone impingement for any specific ADL as the plan is updated' description='Same as [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-614|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-614|smart-link]\n\n\n\nWeb Planner needs to do live calculation to demonstrate the status of bone-bone and implant-implant impingement for all ADLs as implant parameters or anatomy parameters (i.e. SPM classification) are being changed. \n\n* As implant positions move or implant components are changed, calculate impingement possibilities for all ADLs in the background to notify user which ADLs have impingement\n* While impingement calculation is performed, the ADL icons turn grey (rather than red or green) to indicate that the data is being calculated\n* Use pre-calculations for impingement predictions to the extent it is possible to avoid delay in live calculations' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,326 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48500 (CSTEST-614): summary='ADLs1 - Simulation for Activities of Daily living (Skeleton and Patient bone with implants)' description='* As a Surgeon, I would like to know if any of the ADLs will cause impingement risk for my selected implants or implant positions. As I update the implant types/size or their placement, ADLs status should update live (live desired for user experience, in worst case, re-calculate button implementation) with new implants type/size or position. For example, if the standard Anthology stem size 4 was causing impingement, when the standard stem is changed to high offset, if the impingement is resolved the 3D bone model and ADL status icon immediately updates the status to non-impingement. \n\nAdditional details - \n\n* Web Planner needs to display the summary of ADLs impingement status all the time when implant parameters are being adjusted by the user. \n** All ADLs impingement status needs to change live with changes in implant parameters. \n** Areas of impingement are also highlighted all the time on 3D bone model and changes live with changes in implant parameters.\n* The arrangement/placement of the ADLs status needs to be approach specific - Direct Anterior/Posterior Lateral and ability to view all options\n* User is allowed to select any ADLs to view the Motion and impingement details. When a specific ADL is selected, for example Gold Swing, - Simulation of activity/motion (Golf swing) is represented on generic skeleton as well as replicated with patient specific bone model with implant placements. \n** Areas of impingement are highlighted for the user to view.\n** ROM values where impingement occurs are also highlighted. \n* User is allowed to select any of the available ADLs to view the simulation (ROM/Impingement) - Tennis, Golf swing, Yoga, etc,. An individual ADL icon will convey the information of when it is selected/not selected.\n* Web Planner needs to have a predefined set of Femur angles which surgeon can quickly run-through. Ideally, pre-sets are calculated live similar to ADLs. \n\nReferences for additional ADL features -\n\n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-617|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-617|smart-link]\n\n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-651|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-651|smart-link]\n\n\n\n\n\nExample concept as defined below - \n\n!image-20230511-171451.png|width=1452,height=717!\n\n!image-20230511-170355.png|width=1410,height=747!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,326 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48501 (CSTEST-613): summary='IDB harmonization between multiple platforms - Volt, Web portal, (Hip 7?)' description='Web planner will need access to implant surface files/coordinates for display and measurements. Theses files need to match with files being used by Visionaire (VOLT). This feature will identify the process and workflow of managing IDB. Exact list of implants will be determined with further input from Marketing. As default, implant currently supported by RI. Hip modeler needs to be available in the IDB.\n\nDetermine as part of the risk reduction if it needs to match with Hip 7 IDB as well. We are most likely to use the same IDB database for applicable implants (currently used by Hip 7) but need to do this exercise to understand the impact when we decide to add implants which are currently not part of the original database.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,327 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48179 (CSTEST-612): summary='Duplicate tools on same Port in Trackermap.cfg lead to incorrect tracking data' description='[https://gitlab.com/smithandnephew/robotics/Libraries/Tracking/libTrackerAPI/-/blame/0e143684f0bb13d26a90bf02b85e697304e612c5/lib/TAPITracker.cpp?page=2#L1868-1903|https://gitlab.com/smithandnephew/robotics/Libraries/Tracking/libTrackerAPI/-/blame/0e143684f0bb13d26a90bf02b85e697304e612c5/lib/TAPITracker.cpp?page=2#L1868-1903]\n\nJason Cipriani reported (before he left):\n\n_this "gutting" (from 13 years ago), which i just noticed, caught_ [~accountid:622fb5cb442e0e0069ec3440]  _& i off-guard a while back, and it really needs to be ungutted and then tested in production._\n\n_your comment (_[~accountid:5cae259d3318e72736efe8c6] _\'s) reads:_\n\n\n\n{noformat}It seems to be\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0meant to do consistency checking, but the "vpTargets" variable\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0is local, filled, then discarded with no consequence.{noformat}\n\n_but it isn\'t "with no consequence". it throws an exception if the consistency checks fail. that\'s the consequence._\n\n_the entire library is designed around the invariant that no two active trackers share port/vport number but differ in geometry file specifications, and that\'s what that checks._\n\n_without it, a misconfigured trackermap will lead to undetectable tracking errors. if "0 femur 012345.ini" and "0 tibia abcdef.ini" are in the file and are both active, that block of code you gutted causes initialization failure. without it, both are allowed to be activated, but internally they\'ll end up confused with eachother with no consequence except silently incorrect reported positions._\n\n_best case the application crashes; worst case you proceed with ambiguity as to which tracker’s data is being reported._\n\n\n\nThe work to be done for this is to re-enable the “Gutted” code and test it, at least on Atracsys as well as test the use cases which Jason reports should result in an error to ensure they actually give an error.\n\nTesting on Aurora with multi-coil use, which is the reason the offending getAuroraNumPorts() function was added, is likely a long road to hoe, but it would be better to break Aurora functionality than to have someone struggle with erroneous trackermap settings, or even worse, introduce a bug into the product line that randomly works, then all of a sudden doesn’t.' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
