2026-07-20 22:41:52,345 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48508 (CSTEST-604): summary='Implant and Size Selection (Family/Cup/Stem*/Liner/Head*) options' description='The final list of implant types, size, and compatibility will be driven by the configuration of the IDB. Example implants list is below -\n\n*·\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 From the RI HIP Modeler/LifeMOD set:*\n\no\xa0\xa0 R3 cups (NO HOLE, MULTI HOLE, THREE HOLE)\u200b\n\no\xa0\xa0 R3 liners (0 deg, 20 deg, 0 deg +4, 20 deg +4, anteverted, constrained)\u200b\n\no\xa0\xa0 OR3O\u200b\n\no\xa0\xa0 Anthology\u200b + High offset\n\no\xa0\xa0 Synergy\u200b + High offset\n\no\xa0\xa0 Polarstem\u200b\n\no\xa0\xa0 Heads (CoCR, Ox, +Ceramic)\n\n*·\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 From Hip 7.1 set:*\n\no\xa0\xa0 Redapt liners: redapt 0 deg, redapt anteverted\n\no\xa0\xa0 Redapt porous cup\n\no\xa0\xa0 Redapt mod cup\n\no\xa0\xa0 CPCS stem\n\no\xa0\xa0 Redapt stem\n\no\xa0\xa0 Spectron stem\n\n~~~~~~~*~~~~~~~~~~*~~~~~\n\n\n\n*Examples for implant selection -*\n\n!image-20230614-191803.png|width=384,height=318!\n\nExample of RI Hip Modeler implants and compatibility\n\n!image-20230619-154925.png|width=423,height=246!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,346 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48509 (CSTEST-603): summary='Implant (Cup/Stem/Liner) Placement (Rotation/translation) options' description='Web planner allows the user to change position of the implant. Any limitations on the total allowable movement will be determined based on surgical technique or risk assessment. \n\nFeatures to consider positioning flexibility - \n\n|Cup translation - Move cup superior/inferior, medial/lateral, anterior/posterior WRT the pelvis\nAllow 0.25 mm increments/decrements\nCoronal plane - medial/lateral and superior/inferior changes\nTransverse plane - medial/lateral and anterior/posterior changes\nSagittal plane - anterior/posterior and superior/inferior changes|\n|Cup orientation - Rotate cup to change inclination or anteversion WRT the pelvis in both Frontal Pelvic Plane and Anterior Pelvic Plane\nAllow 0.5 degree increments/decrements\nRotation in each plane - Coronal, Axial, Sagittal|\n|Liner orientation (only for Lipped liner) - Rotate liner WRT cup normal axis - Allow 30 degree increments/decrements rotational changes by O’clock position (0-11)|\n|Stem position - Move stem superior/inferior, medial/lateral, anterior/posterior WRT the femur (stem?)\nAllow 0.25 mm increments/decrements\nCoronal plane - medial/lateral and superior/inferior changes\nTransverse plane - medial/lateral and anterior/posterior changes\nSagittal plane - anterior/posterior and superior/inferior changes|\n|Stem orientation - Rotate stem to change angle WRT to femur- anteversion/retroversion, varus/valgus, anterior/posterior tilt\nAllow 0.5 degrees increments/decrements \nRotation in each plane - Coronal, Axial, Sagittal|\n\nView and interaction - Example of 2D cross-section view below. Where user can place the implant in selected plane (coronal/sagittal/transverse) of reference and scroll through the slices to check it’s position w.r.t. bone. Placement arrows help in aligning position and angle. If placement arrows engaged constantly (i.e. Pressed, the movement of implant accelerates). Native and updated COR is always projected in the selected 2D slice.\n\nAbility to expand and shrink the implant plan windows. Ability to zoom pan implant plan (bone/implant).\n\nAny change in the implant position should reflect appropriate changes in the surgical outcome calculations, such as leg length and offset changes, combined anteversion changes, impingement status changes in ADLs.\n\n*Example concept of Cup and Stem placement on a Coronal plane with 2D slices of the 3D models -*\n\n!image-20230614-192629.png|width=388,height=462!\n\n!image-20230614-192606.png|width=264,height=330!' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,350 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48510 (CSTEST-602): summary='Delete  - Case Management' description="{color:#ff5630}*Don’t consider for now.*{color}\n\n{color:#ff5630}*Only consider it if the case management is implemented separately or redundant to Visionaire’s - VCM case management.*{color}\n\nAbility for the user to view currently scheduled cases.\n\nAbility for the user to rearrange cases as pert the scheduled date, patient's first name and last name.  \n\nAbility for the user to view archived or canceled cases and rearrange them\n\n\n\nUsers - Surgeons, Scheduler, SN Rep" issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,352 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48181 (CSTEST-601): summary='Pre-Op Hip Licensing Model' description='Able to follow KPOP structure?… KPOP licensing tied to NSYNC, but HPOP will not have interface with NSYNC from start.\n\n\n\n Typical things to consider - \n\nEvaluate and Confirm scope of Hip Licensing. Are we using Visionaire license? A separate Hip item or combined in any way?\n\nWill license management be linked to VCM/CRM in any way? \n\n\n\nDefinition still pending for the impact to Hip:\n\n* Discussed 06/05/2023: Ability to populate a list of Users, and their selected facilities (selected and assigned to user in NSYNC, by the user), in the VCM. Will need to pull list from NSYNC to populate list in VCM. This can be a manual process in short-term. Eventually, will move to Bridge and Bridge will support licensing. Cumulus/NSYNC can generate the list, but Visionaire will need to cross-check list with onboarded facilities/surgeons. \n** If this manual process is followed, how often will the NSYNC list need to be generated and cross-checked…. Bi-weekly suggested. Alternatively, a Visionaire user can be given access to Cumulus/NSYNC screen to check, but how often would they need to check, and would this be too labor intensive?' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,354 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48182 (CSTEST-600): summary='Pre-Op Hip - Surgeon Planning Portal' description='Overview - The Web Planner displays information of the Engineered Plan created by Visionaire Engineer. Moreover, Web Planner allows surgeon to update the plan by changing implants, or adjusting implants position to achieve desired outcome. Once agreeing to the original/updated plan, surgeon can generate report which can be used intraoperatively by either printing or importing it in CORI Hip7 application.  \n\n*Features-*\n\n# Review Engineered Plan\n# Change implants\n# Update implants positions\n# Review ADLs - summary vs specific activity\n# Review Impingements - bone-bone & implant-implant impingements, summary vs specific activity\n#  Allows free ROM input to review impingements \n# Export final plan in form of reports\n# Reports - can be printed and can be digitally viewed in the OR\n# Reports - contain summary of the plan and additional details and images of bone/dicom ct/' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,355 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48183 (CSTEST-599): summary='Pre-Op Hip - Volt and ADLs/Simulation Application' description='Develop preoperative planner for THA to fit within the Visionaire workflow for use by Visionaire engineers. Planner will be developed as a plugin called VOLTHip within LifeMOD software. Workflow steps required are: \n\n# Import Case \u200b\n# X-ray Measurements:  Spinopelvic lateral x-rays for landmarking and categorization\u200b\n# Preop Measurements:  CT scan+solid bones. Get initial pre-op measures.\xa0\u200b\n# Templating\u200b\n## Cup and Liner templating\u200b\n## Stem and Head templating\u200b\n# Postop Measurements: Capture and visualize changes to alignment\u200b\n# Impingement Analysis: RI Hip Modeler kinematics and 3D impingement\u200b\n# \xa0Case Export: Any necessary data for Web Planner.\n# Hip Implant Database setup and management: Critical piece that needs defined and accessible for both this and the Web Planner\n\n\n\nProgress is tracked on the LifeModeler board in the Hip 3D epic: [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/LIF/boards/92/backlog?selectedEpic=LIF-1148|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/LIF/boards/92/backlog?selectedEpic=LIF-1148|smart-link]' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,356 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48184 (CSTEST-597): summary='Pre-Op Hip - Visionaire Surgeon Onboarding' description='Visionaire offers surgeon-preference driven pre-operative planning solutions. In order to generate pre-operative plans which account for surgeon preferences, Visionaire must meet with each ordering surgeon to capture information regarding their surgical preferences. This activity is considered surgeon onboarding. At the time of surgeon onboarding, surgeons are also asked to provide their imaging center’s information (some may use multiple); the imaging center(s) must be on file with Visionaire.\n\n\n\nScope:\n\nPreference Sheet\n\nDatabase Update to support additional fields captured in CORI-621\n\nQualification of Image Centers\n\nProtocol Development captured in CORI-555' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,356 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48185 (CSTEST-596): summary='RI.INSIGHTS - providing the user (surgeon or staff) the ability to create a patient record in RI.INSIGHTS' description='In the Case List tab, a Plus sign could be added that would allow the user to create a new patient.  PROMs could be added for this patient.  Above/below the comments section should also include a place to upload pre-op plans, images or PDFs.' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
