2026-07-20 22:41:52,386 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48199 (CSTEST-578): summary='Pre-op Planning - Receive Enablement on CORI (Importation - USB)' description="CORI user interface and software design that enables a user (ex: rep) to log in to Admin and initiate pre-operative plan data transfer from a properly formatted USB containing pre-op plan data. CORI 2.0 “Import” button should be leveraged. The system should recognize when a USB is plugged into the system. Reps should be able to select one or multiple KPOP data sets for upload to the system. Reps should be notified (through on screen text vs a dialog box) that download has been completed. \n\nPre-operative plan data sets should be stored on the system so that they are available to be linked to patient cases' at the time of case creation. Pre-op plan data linkage to case covered in [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-567|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-567|smart-link]-.-  4/12: Upon download/upload of pre-operative plan data, patient case will be created automatically. Rep should be notified of this. \n\n----\n\nUse Cases: see attached image\n\nActivity Diagram: see attached image" issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,388 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48200 (CSTEST-577): summary='Pre-Op Planning - Process / Visionaire Outputs' description='Updates to Visionaire tools, processes, outputs to provide CORI with information required to support CORI cases and use of image/plan intraoperatively. \n\nUpdates include: \n\n# Possibly augment Visioniare planning output to be consumed by CORI\n# Visionaire Portal update - need to add dropdown for CORI case (so blocks aren’t made), branding updates\n# Ability to ping MoveMedical/SalesForce for license tracking (usage count)\n# Creating robotics specific onboarding preferences and pre-op plan information/format\n# Osteophyte modeling requirements for robotics cases\n# Use of CORI IDB in VOLT\n# Addition of UKA planning in VOLT (per DD0053)' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
