2026-07-20 22:41:52,390 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48205 (CSTEST-572): summary='Enable new TKA implants to be compatible with Surgeon Personalized Planning' description='With the Release of CORI 2.0, with the introduction of a implantdefaults.json file, any new TKA implant that is added to an IDB after the CORI 2.0 release, will NOT be compatible with Surgeon Personalized Planning (SPP). \n\nThis is because there are 7 reference values that are required to be set for a specific implant design (and deformity bucket) which are not all provided by the IDB (which is what led to the introduction of the implantdefaults.json to enable the SPP feature in CORI 2.0).\n\nThe 7 preference values for a *Varus* preoperative deformity are:\n\n# Femur component V/v\n# Femur distal _lateral_ resection\n# Femur posterior medial resection\n# Femur posterior lateral resection\n# Tibia component V/v\n# Tibia component slope\n# Tibia _lateral_ resection\n\nThe 7 preference values for a *Valgus* preoperative deformity are:\n\n# Femur component V/v\n# Femur distal _medial_ resection\n# Femur posterior medial resection\n# Femur posterior lateral resection\n# Tibia component V/v\n# Tibia component slope\n# Tibia _medial_ resection\n\nThe only preference values that could be pulled directly from the IDB FM0049 (for a particular implant) are:\n\n# Femur component V/v\n# Tibia component V/v\n# Tibia component slope\n# Tibia lateral resection\n\nThus, as part of the CORI 2.0 project the implantdefaults.json was created to fill in these missing values.  These default values were provided by the Marketing Team for each of the 9 TKA implants compatible with CORI that existed at the time of the CORI 2.0 project. The defaults provided were based on manual surgical technique as specified in the S+N implant surgical technique guides. The 9 implants are:\n\n# Journey II XR\n# Journey II CR\n# Journey II BCS\n# Legion CR\n# Legion PS\n# Genesis II PS\n# Genesis II CR\n# Anthem PS\n# Legion Porous CR\n\nIf a future TKA implant is added to a CORI IDB, that implant will NOT be compatible with SPP without a Software Update.\n\nThe CORI 2.0 brainstormed potential partial solutions to mitigate this, but all options introduced technical debt and had the potential to be confusing for end users so none were pursued. These partial solutions included:\n\n* Setting a set of generic “backup” default values to use in the instance when a new implant is added that is not in the implantdefaults.json.\n** The team would have implemented Journey default values since the next new TKA implant to be used with CORI will most likely fall in the Journey implant family.\n** Main Issue: If the next implant were NOT Journey, the default values displayed to the user would be evidently wrong.  This would also cause the definition of what these values represent to be wrong.\n* Implement the concept of “Implant Families” (as determined by the implant name) and have “backup” default values specific to the implant family.\n** Main Issue: There is no formal concept of Implant Families as defined in the IDB. Thus, the team would be making an assumption around what an implant family is without any formal guidance.\n** Additional Issue: This still would not cover scenarios in which a new implant were added that does not fall into the existing implant design “families”, i.e. Journey, Legion, Genesis, etc. Along these same lines, this would not cover any test IDBs in which the implant names do not fall into these categories either.\n* Calculate the preference values we can from the IDB for any new implant not present in the implantdefaults.json file.\n** This would involve pulling existing code from intraop and using it in Launcher (fairly risky)\n** Main Issue: This would introduce potential dependencies between the Software and the IDB that do not currently exist.\n** Other Issues:\n*** The calculated values would not be “true defaults” even if they would be close\n*** There is no reasonable way to determine Tibia medial resection depth from this method so there would either need to be a missing value with additional logic to ensure the user edits this value before they can save a preference OR you would need to have some systematic way to choose a value (i.e. apply the lateral RD to also be the medial) which would be inherently wrong in some cases.\n\n\n\nThe best long term solution would likely be an IDB process update.  For instance, it could be required moving forward, to include the implant default values as part of the IDB and these values could be read directly by CORI to be used in SPP (and the implantdefaults.json would be eliminated).' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,391 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48206 (CSTEST-571): summary='Sports Med PRIME Integration on Cumulus' description='Sports Med will be using the RI.Insights infrastructure to store Prime and FAI case data. The ask is to distribute the related end point on the file transfer service to allow Sports Med data storage in Ri.Insights DocumentDB and S3 Buckets. \n\nThose were created on the R&D Cloud but must be integrated into the production deployment inline with Prime release (early 2024)\n\nThere is no UI changes or impact on the current features, this process is only to provide data storage support for Prime, data in DocumentDB will be separated from CORI data, S3 bucket is dedicated to Sports Med.\n\nTwo services are required, but the AnalyticLogger service is already part of the Ri,Insights, The addition to the Pre-Signed URL service is the only augmented service.\n\nA new ClientID/ClientSecret identification must be created in order for the sports med devices to authenticate with those services.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,393 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48207 (CSTEST-570): summary='Enhanced Implant Planning Logs' description='Create a logging feature that tracks a user’s “clicks” (i.e. button presses) while they’re in Combined Planning.  This should allow S+N R&D to better understand HOW end users approach / go through Planning and their workflow to place an implant.\n\n*The types of data that would be beneficial to log include:*\n\n* Metadata\n** Case ID\n** Surgeon ID\n** Software Version\n** Initial implant selected on case start\n* Surgeon “Characterization” Data\n** Do they use Personalized Planning (SPP), i.e. do they have a saved preference\n** Do they collect joint laxity, i.e. in Surgeon Preferences have they set Joint Laxity to “Collect”\n*** Did they collect both pre-op and post-op gap data\n*** Did they use a tensioner to collect gap data, i.e. the used gaps were from a tensioner collection\n*** How many times does the user navigate back to gap assessment or clear collected gaps\n*** Future: what do they use for tensioner (PCL retractor, Z retractor, true manual, tensioner, competitor tensioning device)\n* Patient “Characterization” Data\n** Pre-operative deformity (long leg alignment V/v, flexion contracture, etc.) → beneficial to record every time the user enters planning\n** Is it a revision case? Did they have previous hardware that needed to be removed at the time of surgery?\n* Workflow data\n** {color:#4c9aff}Entry and exit into planning (include time stamps){color}\n** {color:#4c9aff}Updates to implant position{color}\n** {color:#4c9aff}Changing implant design{color}\n** {color:#4c9aff}Changing implant size (poly thickness included){color}\n** {color:#4c9aff}The collected preop gaps (max gaps in every flexion bin, both medial and lateral) that are being used in Planning (with 1.7.0.0 there are "used gaps" files{color}\n*** {color:#4c9aff}Look at NTKR_PreOpMedialChosenFlexionGapData, NTKR_PreOpLateralChosenFlexionGapData{color}\n*** {color:#4c9aff}Include Tensioner vs. Manual flag{color}\n** {color:#4c9aff}What state the user navigates to/from{color}\n** {color:#4c9aff}How many times is user viewing SPP intraop window while in Planning{color}\n*** {color:#4c9aff}What reference file the user has selected in SPP intraop (and if they change that selection){color}\n**** {color:#4c9aff}What data is in the ref file selected?{color}\n** Final postop gaps\n** Final implant design and size recorded in the case review screen\n\n*Data to include with each implant position update / click:*\n\n* "click_femur_inferior" → every click should have a descriptive key → like the button ID\n* Implant Placement Values (12 numbers)\n* Calculated postop results (i.e. postop flexion ROM and long leg V/v)\n* When change implant design or size record the same values\n\nIt is also important to time stamp the different actions performed in order to recreate the user’s planning workflow. All data that a time stamp should be included is indicated by {color:#4c9aff}blue text{color} above.\n\nIf the implementation is a new file, it should be encrypted. This would be a backend only update that is not user facing.\n\nSome code was generated originally as part of the CORI 2.0 team on a separate branch which can be found in [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/RIOSI-1399|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/RIOSI-1399|smart-link] (linked below) which can be used and built upon or just used as an initial reference.\n\n\n\nOther things to consider:\n\n* How big the file may become\n** Does it have the potential to change the worst case scenario max Case size\n* Will writing to the file introduce lag of any kind\n* How to organize the data to ensure it is useable' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,394 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48208 (CSTEST-569): summary='Pre-Op Planning- Use of Pre-Op Data in Bone Removal' description='UPDATE ON 4/11 - SEE REGISTRATION EPIC (CORI-568) - With decision to wrap the Visionaire 3D anatomical bone models with the atlas mesh, is there a need to consider changes to Bone Removal? The Bone Removal state may not be subject to any changes. \n\nRequires building workpiece from the registered, patient-specific 3D anatomical model segmented pre-operatively from the patient’s radiological images. Should assess implications of registration accuracy (CORI-568) on Bone Removal state. Should assess look of workpiece/model and understand implications on user experience (i.e. consider similarities/differences between image-free and image-based representations for both TKA and UKA).' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,403 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48209 (CSTEST-568): summary='Pre-Op Planning - Registration of Pre-Op Plan/Image Data' description='Add functionality for image-based registration.\n\nRegistration encompasses all of the updates necessary within the CORI intraoperative application to enable 3D anatomical models (segmented from the patient’s radiological images), along with the pre-operatively planned implant positions, to be registered to the position of the patient’s physical, corresponding anatomy, intraoperatively. The segmented 3D anatomical models should exist in or be traceable to their original positions in the raw image data space, enabling simultaneous display of the 3D anatomical models, planned implant positions (with respect to their positions on the 3D anatomical models), and radiological images (i.e. DICOM image stack), intraoperatively.  \n\nWith regard to pre-operatively planned cases where patient-specific image data, including segmented 3D anatomical models and planned implant positions, are uploaded to the CORI intraoperative application, CORI free collection should facilitate registration, as opposed to facilitating atlas model generation. \n\nThe patient’s 3D anatomical models should be displayed in the CORI registration phase.  The addition of an intraoperative registration accuracy check or registration verification phase/state should be considered. Consider leveraging comparison of landmark positions generated within the CORI reference frame to corresponding landmark positions generated (following the same methods/algorithms) on the patient’s 3D anatomical models.\n\nThe patient’s 3D anatomical models and their registered positions should be used/displayed within the CORI intraoperative implant planning states (see CORI-574), live bone states (i.e. gap assessment models and post-op assessment models), and bone removal states (see CORI-569). The use/display of the registered 3D anatomical models in the live bone states is captured within the scope of this Epic.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,404 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48210 (CSTEST-567): summary='Pre-Op Planning - Workflow Selector' description="Assumption: Pre-operative plan data sets should be stored on the system so that they are available to be linked to patient cases' at the time of case creation. (Ref CORI-578, CORI-551)\n\n\nThis feature includes UI/functionality to:\n\n# Link pre-op plan data to patient case at time of case creation.(See [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-551|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-551|smart-link] for scoping)\n# Based on linkage of pre-op plan data to a case, trigger workflow states, calculation differences, backend information use specific to pre-op plan type cases. \n# “Turn off” SPP\n\n----\n\nIdentify a case as imaged based so that the following can happen:\n\n* Ignore preferences having to do with implant positioning\n* Use Visionaire to CORI implant mapping coordinate system (see [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-568|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-568|smart-link], CORI-574\n* Use of pre-op plan data (bone model STL, component position/size information) (see [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-568|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-568|smart-link], [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-569|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-569|smart-link], CORI-574) \n* Adapt log files as necessary to accommodate added information from image/pre-op plan (see CORI-575)" issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,405 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48211 (CSTEST-566): summary='CORI 2.1 - Quality Improvements' description='Integration of the following Defects completed by POST Development:\n\n*BUGZILLA ID:* \n\n|1798|Intraop crashes upon transition into Handpiece Connection state|\n|1823|In KPC reports table, random exposure value is being reported as zero|\n|1885|The BurSelection back to BoneRemoval fails if not advancing in BurLoading after unlocking|\n|1894|TestEnglish Discrepancy in Tracker visibility section|\n|1903|Bone model not visible on entering femur bur initial cut from bur all mode|\n|1904|M-L letters not aligned on arrows in UKA Adjust ML screen|\n|1907|Femur Neutral Position title is reflecting on Femur Kinematic Axis screen while implementing backward navigation|\n|1949|Characters become skewed in the Case Info screen when adding spaces to fields|\n|1962|The "Edit" buttons have gotten smaller causing cut-off text 3 languages|\n|1963|Cannot reliably open a newly created case in Dutch|\n|1973|Error notification "pedal cable disconnected" displayed in bone removal|\n|1974|On resumed case the femur knee Centre disappeared: backward navigation till Surgeon preference and then forward navigation|\n|1981|Flooding logs with "Tool not IDENTIFIED" exceptions when HP is not connected|\n|1987|Incorrect validation position setting in HAD|\n|1993|Spotted tibia mesh occasionally appears in initial Planning screenshots|\n|1999|Special Points are not retained after system throws internal error|\n|2001|Overcut occurring around same time as System Time Out error|\n|2017|Tibia Bone Model did not save, user had to recollect|\n|2019|Export button disabled in the Include Sensitive Information pop-up window|\n|2022|Internal Error occurring during Checkpoint Definition or Checkpoint Verification|\n|2028|GLTK_Value::operator functions not doing what they think they are doing|\n|2030|high-confidence region of bone is not rendered properly in certain stages|\n|2048|Random exposure value is being reported as zero in Handpiece Diagnostics Application|\n|2049|Max stop time and max retraction time display incorrect minimum values in HDA Operative App, and max stop time passes with bur not spinning|\n|2053|After recollection and reentering combined planning state implant sizes are changing to random values in initial node|\n|2092|"Pedal Cable Disconnected" error notification displayed in various screens during TP1432 execution|' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
