2026-07-20 22:41:52,415 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48220 (CSTEST-555): summary='Pre-Op Visionaire Planning Infrastructure - Hip' description='Patient-specific, pre-operative surgical planning requires specific processes and procedures be put in place to enable surgeons and other clinicians to request and receive plans. The infrastructure must facilitate surgeon/clinician ordering, radiological image uploading, image processing, plan generation, and plan reporting. The infrastructure must consider quality control and quality assurance measures, and it must ensure traceability of each patient’s case. The infrastructure must also accommodate surgeon planning preferences. \n\nSee link below for System Architecture Diagram:  \n\n[Hip Pre-op Planning workflow and tools.pptx|https://smithandnephew.sharepoint.com/:p:/r/sites/Pre-OpSurgicalPlanning/Shared%20Documents/HIP/03_Design%20Inputs/Hip%20Pre-op%20Planning%20workflow%20and%20tools.pptx?d=wfd92447614f94e8baa61cc3e38e6d426&csf=1&web=1&e=jiqF3z]' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,419 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48221 (CSTEST-554): summary='Pre-Op Planning Cloud Infrastructure - Knee' description='This would be some cloud repository & staging area for plan data (as it exits the Visionaire pipeline) and is prepared for download to CORI.\n\nPlan and image (.stl) need to be able to be uploaded to a repository and CORI (or user) needs to be able to pull from this repository for use in a case.\n\nIncludes technical effort, as well as process creation required to implement E2E process (plan complete from engineering to use in case). \n\nThis includes evaluation of cybersecurity requirements (file encryption and/or removal of PHI), data identification plan (underlying and user facing based on Visionaire process).' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,419 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48222 (CSTEST-553): summary='UKR Stressed ROM Workflow and Display Like TKA' description='To improve consistency and efficiency the UKR application, Stressed ROM collection states should be updated to match the TKA application display and workflow.  This also includes the UKR non-stressed collection.  Current images and workflow below for reference.\n\n!image-20221013-154817.png|width=461,height=260!\n\n^TKA Gap Assessment (stressed ROM)\n\n!image-20221013-154841.png|width=467,height=263!\n\nTKA Flexion Range (non-stressed/kinematic axis collection)\n\n!image-20221013-154919.png|width=425,height=260!\n\n^UKR Stressed ROM (Gap Assesment)\n\n!image-20221013-154930.png|width=436,height=283!\n\n^UKR Kinematic Axis (non-stressed)\n\n!image-20221013-155015.png|width=504,height=376!\n\n!image-20221013-155031.png|width=504,height=388!' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,421 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48223 (CSTEST-552): summary='UKR Gap Display Like TKA' description='To give the TKA and UKR applications a consistent look and feel the illustrations conceptualizing ligament balance should match.  Today The UKR application displays gap data in horizontal line-graph format (X-axis is flexion).   The TKA application uses bars on a horizontal graph.  The two applications should converge to a single format.  \n\n!image-20221013-151230.png|width=474,height=268!\n\n!NUKR-19-06-2019-15609439007-A-PlanProsthesisGap-20190619-203414.jpg|width=50%!\n\n^it’s a Navio screen.. but you get the idea.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,423 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48224 (CSTEST-551): summary='Pre-op Planning - Receive Enablement on CORI (Importation - Cloud)' description="CORI user interface and software design that enables a user (ex: rep) to log in to Admin and initiate pre-operative plan data transfer from robotic cloud API platform (Lumino pre-op plan case repository). CORI 2.0 “Import” button should be leveraged. The rep should be able to specify via a user interface element that the data download is to happen via connectivity from Lumino (pre-op plan case repository). Reps should be able to select one or multiple KPOP data sets for download on the system. Reps should be notified (through on screen text vs a dialog box) that download has been completed. \n\nPre-operative plan data sets should be stored on the system so that they are available to be linked to patient cases' at the time of case creation. Pre-op plan data linkage to case covered in [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-567|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-567|smart-link]-.-  4/12: Upon download/upload of pre-operative plan data, patient case will be created automatically. Rep should be notified of this. \n\n----\n\nUse Cases: see attached image\n\nActivity Diagram: see attached image" issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
