2026-07-20 22:41:52,479 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48258 (CSTEST-504): summary='Implantation of RIOS hybrid architecture to TKA states' description='Creation of the RI.OS hybrid architecture and begin leveraging the hybrid architecture in the following states of the CORI TKA procedure:\n\n* Free Collection\n* Combined Planning\n* Pre-Op Gap Assessment\n* Post-Op Gap Assessment\n* Case Review' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,479 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48259 (CSTEST-503): summary='RIOS Initial SDK' description='This project will include the initial RI.OS SDK release, which will introduce the RI.OS based componentized framework that will enable the migration to a long-term RI.OS platform. Introducing the RI.OS components that will be integrated with existing software in a hybrid approach will \xa0ease migration of all CORI software applications to the RI.OS platform in the long run.\xa0\xa0 In addition to Surgeon Preferential Planning, the TKA states of free collection, combined planning, gap assessment (pre-op and post-op), and case review will be updated to leverage the RI.OS components in a hybrid solution.\xa0\xa0 The function and end user experience for these states will not change; changes will be made just to the underlying implementation.\xa0\xa0 This initial RIOS SDK release will also enable new applications such as FAI and Shoulder to be constructed in a manner that will support long term RIOS' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,480 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48260 (CSTEST-502): summary='UI/UX upgrades to RI.KNEE' description='This effort is to perform some enhancement to UI/UX in RI.KNEE to make a number of change to improve the UI/UX interfaces.   \n\nSummary of UI updates: \n\n* UI icons in CORI Application that are not related to Critical Tasks to be updated\n* Screen titles in Application will be moved to the Left Hand Side (LHS) of the screen\n* Fonts in the Application will be updated to comply with S+N branding guidelines\n* Look and feel of the Footpedal UI elements will be updated to rectangular shapes\n* “Quit” or “Exit” icon moved to support titles moving to top LHS' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
