2026-07-20 22:41:52,574 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48546 (CSTEST-396): summary='ActiveArm: Software Aided Soft Tissue Protection for Saw End Effector' description='When using a saw end effector [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412|smart-link] with the active arm both visibility and tactile feedback within the knee are limited compared to using a saw during a manual procedure.  The active arm software should aid in preventing the user from damaging soft tissue structures within the knee.  \n\nThese structures include:\n\n* Popliteal Artery\n* Patellar Tendon\n* MCL\n* LCL \n* PCL\n* ACL\n\nResults from a survey of 19 orthopedic surgeons are below\n\n!image-20211123-201204.png|width=1221,height=522!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
