2026-07-20 22:41:52,579 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48556 (CSTEST-390): summary='RKA: Point Probe Refinement Tool' description='CAD Attached. Sam Dumpe was MechE\n\nHardware component which fits onto the end of the point probe and can be used to refine the virtual workpiece \n\nAs seen in CAD, hardware is analogous to the plane visualizer without the plane at the end. Considerations on-going about extending length of shaft.\n\nMust haves/do:\n\n* Must connect to point probe\n* Utilize same vendor as plane visualizer\n\nSurgeons have validated use of this tool for the above intended purpose.\n\nTray insert or brackets are not in scope for this tool.' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,580 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48309 (CSTEST-377): summary='VoC - Allow 9-30mm (8-30mm for XR) Polys selection in TKA' description='*UPDATE* - Alex Czamara, 06/20/2022\n\nAdd a mechanism to case review screen for updating poly thicknesses for all implant designs separately from the polys available in the IDB.\n\n* All implant designs (except for XR) will have a range of *9-30mm* poly thickness options, with *1mm increment*s.\n* For XR, the range will be *8-30mm*, with *1mm increments*. \n\nThis will encompass every possible thickness across all S+N implant designs.\n\nNote: On entry to the Case Review screen, we will continue to display the implant size and poly thickness that was originally selected in the Combined Planning stage. If the user changes the poly thickness, it will NOT carry over into Planning.\n\nProposed solution outline in table below:\n\n!image-20220620-205005.png|width=584,height=289!\n\n----\n\n*ORIGINAL TICKET*\n\n1mm increment polys for Gen II and LEGION are only clinically and commercially available in high-flex, deep dish (CR) or constrained (PS). CORI models the standard poly configurations, which are available in 9,11,13,15 \\[..]mm. \n\n\n\nCurrent Poly Sizes for each implant line:\n\n!anthem.PNG|width=50%,alt="Anthem Inserts"!\n\n!Gen II inserts.PNG|width=257,height=161,alt="Gen II inserts"!\n\n!Journey II inserts.PNG|width=256,height=78,alt="Journey II inserts"!\n\n!Legion inserts.PNG|width=278,height=137,alt="Legion inserts"!\n\n!image-20211116-161942.png|width=488,height=141,alt="XR inserts (same across all baseplate sizes)"!\n\n\n\nOld Title: “Add a mechanism to case review for updating LEGION and Gen II poly thickness to account for missing 10 and 12 mm polys in IDB”' issueType='Epic' status="Won't Do" parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,581 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48310 (CSTEST-376): summary='Collection of Post-Op ROM (proposed update to current algorithm)' description='Currently CORI tracks the post-op ROM throughout the post-operative screens and ultimately displays the maximum extension and maximum flexion value detected by the system whenever trackers are visible. The value displayed on the case review screen is not representative of the footpedal captured data but of the max extension and max flexion seen by the trackers. \n\nThere are various point in time when the trackers may be visible on the Femur and Tibia but there are not trial components in the joint, and this can lead to skewed reporting in the case review screen (i.e. extreme hyperextension)\n\nWe have received a number of questions and points of field feedback on this topic and would like to suggest we update the functionality of the software to be more representative of the information the surgeon is choosing to collect. Based on feedback, we would like to collect the post-op flexion range from last footpedal driven collection in the baseline state. This implementation is analogous in nature to our pre-op flexion range of motion collection (range of motion), and will allow the user to determine when and what range of motion is collected. \n\nThis should eliminate skewed data visible on the case review screen. Moreover, this information will be transitioned to RI.INSIGHTS (data management platform) and can be referenced by the surgeon after cases are completed. \n\nHave attached the first FR, and there has been further feedback provided to the team, mainly from the ANZ market, but also from select US sites.' issueType='Epic' status="Won't Do" parent=None
