2026-07-20 22:41:52,597 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48322 (CSTEST-363): summary='UKR Free Collection Update' description='Bring UKR Free Collection State up to date with TKA.  Features include:\n\nMust have - auto-rotate the screen as user collects\n\nMust have - Add special point collection\n\nNice to have (unless needed for less discrete collection) - Add critical regions to UKA\n\nMust have - registration regions for UKA in IB\n\nMust have - Removal of green points as default\n\nMust have - Show whole bone when painting\n\nNice to have - wider Paint Brush - maybe not 5mm but bigger.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,599 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48323 (CSTEST-362): summary='Registered trials within the Robotics Workflow (+update post-op gaps with this info)' description='Support registration of trial components (femur and tibia) within the Robotics workflow. The implant teams, starting with Sync instrumentations, are generating trial components with divots to allow for registration in the Robotic workflow (divots are the dimension and shape of CORI point probe and locations and dimensions were integrated in conjunction with Robotics team). \n\nUpon registering trial components, surgeons can assess position, rotation, etc which are not set by CORI, and can prep fixation features for implants accordingly. \n\nThis registration can also be used (in conjunction with entering a poly thickness) for final gap assessment to remove dependency on baseline collection for determining post-operative gaps. This is particularly valuable for use with tensioner, as currently the baseline collection does not contain any information today with the tensioner thickness.' issueType='Epic' status='Define' parent=None
