2026-07-20 22:41:52,609 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48560 (CSTEST-339): summary='RKA: Data export support for RKA - for import into Data Management Platform' description='Revision Knee Application\n\nData export to align with updated export for TKA and UKR in format and process. Data needs to be able to be consumed by RI.INSIGHTS. \n\nAll current data fields exported in TKA remain applicable. \n\nAdditional data fields for reporting can include: augment selections (size and location), joint line measurements. \n\n* Added data fields have been discussed with the R+D teams and information exists in EA or with SYS ENG teams from prior discussions. \n\nPlease see MVP field for minimum fields to be exported\n\nNice to Have:\n\nImage export from procedure (realistic model and relative location of reference point(s)) to indicate location of joint line reference on either the femur or the tibia\n\n* This can also be implemented with stock image in post-processing (upload) \n* Inclusion of image to be determined based on implementation prototypes and user feedback' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,610 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48561 (CSTEST-338): summary='RKA: Bone Refinement in Registration' description='This feature describes a need to create a surface which approximates the post explant tibia bone surface. The post-explant bone surface needs to be referenced during planning and also needs to be used to create a volumentric cutting model for bone removal.\n\nThis feature is needed for addition of RKA functionality. Upon completion of point collection in free collection, the software needs to create a volumetric model that can be refined to depict the surface of the bone once the original implant is removed. This will be used during planning to visualize.\nThis has a dependency on the hardware that will be used to refine: using the CORI handpiece to refine or using the CORI pointer probe with a new refining guard.\n\nSimilar to the bone refinement stage in F/T bone removal, however, we need to have this stage prior to final planning.\n\n# Creation of a volumetric model upon collection of sufficient free collection points.\n# Potentially select tool used for refining or determine based on proximity to the bone.\n# Allow for refining using handpiece\n# Allow also for refining using the pointer probe \\[Need to connect with the HW team to get the dimensions]\n# \n\n\nRevision MVP;\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt]' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,610 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48562 (CSTEST-337): summary='RKA: Joint Line Reference' description='Revision MVP;\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/LSycnp|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/LSycnp|smart-link]' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,612 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48563 (CSTEST-336): summary='RKA: Augment Planning' description='Revision MVP; EA and Prolaborate boards detail technical implementation and state position in workflow. Once augments are selected, augment choices to be maintained if HCP goes back to planning. \n\nAugment planning should use augment implant CAD.\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/LmCqqG|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/LmCqqG|smart-link]' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,612 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48564 (CSTEST-335): summary='RKA: Workflow Selection for Revision (intraoperative workflow selection)' description='Means to enable features associated with revision knee procedure, upon installation:\n\n# Means to enable the feature set (akin to total knee features enabling)\n# Means to confirm user has purchased the feature set (additional line in code)\n# Means to install Revision Implant (LEGION RK, plus augments) via the terminal.\n\nMeans to include enabled features in case workflow for Revision Procedures:\n\n# (1) Case Creation Screen\n## Procedure: TKA\n## Implant: LEGION RK\n# Surgeon Preferences Screen\n## Joint Laxity: Collect / Skip\n## Initial Implant Planning: Yes / No\n## Femur Rotational Reference: PCA / Manually Define\n## Tibia Resection: Default / +1 /+2 / +3\n## Femur Implant Referencing : Anterior / Posterior\n## {color:#ff5630}SDIP: Yes / No – TBD how implemented (not a current selection, but may be there when RKA is launched){color}\n## Rotation Center (Femur): Medial Posterior / Knee Center\n## {color:#ff5630}Femur Cut Selection: Distal Bur / Bur all (not a current selection, but may be there when RKA is launched){color}\n## Joint Line: Femur / Tibia / Both / None\n# \n\nAll preferences are available for all procedures.Selection of LEGION RK implant drives inclusion of Bone Refinement (F/T) between initial implant planning and gap assessment. Upon leaving implant planning, system will read last implant selected, should it be LEGION RK, Augment Planning will appear.If features are enabled, all should be accessed from Other Options button (joint line, refinement, augment planning).If you change implants from TKA to RK, system will prompt user to complete bone refinement stages.\n\nRevision MVP; EA and prolaborate boards describe how surgeon is able to select and complete a procedure with the added implants and added features. EA also depicts state transitions and logic for completion of workflow. \n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Repository/Artifact.aspx?repId=99685971-6983-427d-b366-71a2193839f9&procId=\\{0DF2F9FE-2CE4-4b1f-AD7D-032121352404}|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Repository/Artifact.aspx?repId=99685971-6983-427d-b366-71a2193839f9&procId=%7B0DF2F9FE-2CE4-4b1f-AD7D-032121352404%7D]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Repository/Artifact.aspx?Auth=w4fM9d73biPACn1Y31nJea%2fIjg9%2fqn62Ua%2bA2zypNpLpsO6bl8FY2UJdLM7Sw9cW3iiXIsEvN9PzgBGKs9%2buLoP3CkXklhuQJ%2bSAx%2b0kK0KHenbGvi8ZzT%2f3AbgMjqXeQPw2ph2lkqV0Kt2N43faCZIoPl7dzBeRw87ZIHlPH3oq8PF%2bEeqGtqkQ9UkOSZ3x|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Repository/Artifact.aspx?Auth=w4fM9d73biPACn1Y31nJea%2fIjg9%2fqn62Ua%2bA2zypNpLpsO6bl8FY2UJdLM7Sw9cW3iiXIsEvN9PzgBGKs9%2buLoP3CkXklhuQJ%2bSAx%2b0kK0KHenbGvi8ZzT%2f3AbgMjqXeQPw2ph2lkqV0Kt2N43faCZIoPl7dzBeRw87ZIHlPH3oq8PF%2bEeqGtqkQ9UkOSZ3x|smart-link] \n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt]' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-20 22:41:52,612 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48565 (CSTEST-334): summary='RKA: Create Revision IDB configuration' description='Add Revision components into our IDB structure. This includes the following Femur/Tibia configurations:\n\n# LEGION RK Femur / RK (constrained) Poly / LEGION RK Tibia\n# LEGION PS Femur / PS Poly / LEGION RK Tibia  ?\n# LEGION PS Femur / PS Poly / LEGION Primary Tibia\n\nThese combinations should support what would be considered standard poly. On PS tibia we should support the PS poly.  for RK we should support the RK poly.  \n\nAll to be compatible with augments per the implant designs (i.e. LEGION RK Femur, LEGION RK Tibia and LEGION PS femur are compatible)\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt]\n\nAdditional information on IDB configurations, start to WI0040 process and compatibility, among other topics, can be found in MM and meeting notes from prior sessions with team (Mike C, Dave D, Kavya, Mara)' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
