2026-07-21 00:03:07,932 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48175 (CSTEST-624): summary='Materialise Mimics for CT Segmentation' description='As part of the Hip Pre-operative Planning workflow, once CT images are uploaded and reviewed for quality purposes, they must be processed to produce 3D models of the patient’s bone anatomy; this process is called Segmentation. Several segmentation applications exist on the market. An assessment of these products was conducted to support selection of Materialise Mimics. \n\nSegmentation Vendor Assessment: \n\n[https://smithandnephew-my.sharepoint.com/:x:/g/personal/april_krivoniak_smith-nephew_com/ERNrH23OmD9Lr67npLF1cj4BZ7R_4t13qyUKTQHiphnUAQ?e=xdKlhy|https://smithandnephew-my.sharepoint.com/:x:/g/personal/april_krivoniak_smith-nephew_com/ERNrH23OmD9Lr67npLF1cj4BZ7R_4t13qyUKTQHiphnUAQ?e=xdKlhy|smart-link] \n\nThe Visionaire team is familiar with Materialise Mimics and holds several license seats of the software. The team will update to the latest version of the software to support the hip pre-operative planning workflow. \n\n\n\nLicense Needs: Mimics25 & MedCad' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:07,932 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48176 (CSTEST-623): summary='VIVS for Hip Imaging QC - PreOp Planning' description='UPDATED 4/28 - Segaway identified as alternative tool which can support image review processes and procedures for hip pre-operative planning. Segaway is an opensource, web-based, medical imaging viewer which supports all imaging modalities, including CT and X-ray (necessary for hip). VIVS does not support CT. See [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-622|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-622|smart-link]. \n\n\n\nAppropriate changes to VIVS software or provide an alternative which can support following - \n\nImport Dicom images CT/Xray\n\nVerify Image quality for parameters like\n\nPatient Name, DOB, Surgical side\n\nScan date\n\nCT protocols - Field of View, Scale, Slice thickness/interval, reconstruction algorithms, disturbance due to movement or metals\n\nXray protocols - Field of view, Scale, disturbance due to movement or metals' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:07,933 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48177 (CSTEST-622): summary='Segaway for Image Review' description='After upload of patient images to the VCM, the uploaded images are transferred to the patient’s case folder. The images must be reviewed to ensure they meet pre-defined, required specifications and to ensure all necessary images have been uploaded. Erroneous images must be removed from the patient’s case folder. Image review shall occur in a medical image viewer. Segaway is an open-source, web-based, medical imaging viewer used by Visionaire today. Segaway has the ability to view images of any modality. Segaway lacks features tailored Visionaire-specific needs, and these features are necessary to support image review at scale. Segaway also lacks the features which facilitate knee-specific image generation and automated migration of these generated files (VIVS currently supports knee-specific image review processes).' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:07,933 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48178 (CSTEST-621): summary='VCM UI: User Login, Case Creation, and Case Management' description='The addition of the Hip Pre-operative Planning offering will require a new patient case “Type” to be added in the VCM (Visionaire Customer Management portal), along with subsequent portal updates that capture Hip Pre-operative Planning case information and surgical preference details. Changes will need to propagate to the CRM (customer relationship management) portion of the overarching VCM.\n\nPortal branding considerations needed for the addition of Pre-operative Hip Planning. \n\n\n\nUse Case(s): \n\n* A portal for Surgeon/clinician ordering of pre-operative hip plans.\n* A portal for Surgeon/clinician image upload to support pre-operative hip planning.\n* A portal for Surgeon/clinician review of pre-operative hip plans.\n* A portal for Surgeon/clinician request of updates to pre-operative hip plans.\n* A platform for Visionaire to manage customers of pre-operative hip planning, + their imaging centers.\n* A platform for Visionaire to manage pre-operative hip planning cases throughout the workflow\n\n\n\n* Likely external portal users include: Surgeons, Schedulers, SN Reps, Imaging center technicians\n* Likely internal portal users include: Visionaire Support team members, Visionaire Image Reviewers, Visionaire Segmenters, Visionaire Engineers' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
