2026-07-21 00:03:07,946 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48502 (CSTEST-610): summary='Measurements display for reference' description='Web planner needs to match the definition of measurements with VOLT so they represent same values in VOLT plan and Web plan. All the calculations are performed for the operating leg. Leg length/offset is also calculated for the non-operating leg. The measurements needs to be calculated based on the landmarks provided by VOLT plan and implants. \n\nConsider following examples - \n\n# Spinopelvic classification/ (tilt?) - (No live measurements, only display) - Only measured on VOLT but web planner displays it and allows the user to override/change it. ADL impingement status and respective implant measurements will change accordingly to match the change.\n## SPM Classification - Allowed to override\n## Standing Pelvic Tilt - Allowed to override\n# Cup anteversion and inclination - Web planner displays the information as pet VOLT plan and allows users to change it. ADL impingement status and respective implant measurements will change accordingly to match the change.\n# Stem anteversion/retroversion rotations - Web planner displays the information as pet VOLT plan and allows users to change it. ADL impingement status and respective implant measurements will change accordingly to match the change.\n# Leg length and offset - Resultant of the change in cup and stem types/placements. Computed and displayed. Compared with native and opposite leg.\n# COR shifts - Resultant of the change in cup/stem positions. Computed and displayed. Compared against native and opposite leg. \n# Combined version - Addition of the cup and stem version values. Computed/displayed. \n# Neck cut height - Distance between two landmarks. landmark 1 may be provided by VOLT. Landmark 2 will be determined based on the neck cut plane (intersection of medial one and cut plane). Compute/display.\n# Medial wall distance - distance between cup apex and medial acetabulum wall. Compute and display.\n# Cup overhang - Cup edge from anterior acetabulum rim point. Compute and display.\n\nExample-\n\n!image-20230512-131333.png|width=725,height=263!' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:07,946 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48503 (CSTEST-609): summary='Implant Reference system - FP and APP' description='Web planner need to support following reference systems as some surgeons would like to use one vs another.  The cup orientation values should be represented in the selected reference plane. \n\n# FP - Frontal (Coronal) Plane\n# APP - Anterior Pelvic Plane\n\nVOLT will provide the landmarks and initial definition of these planes. User on the Web planner will be allowed to select one vs another and the display of respective measurement values will change accordingly.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:07,947 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48504 (CSTEST-608): summary='Visualization - Bone/Implants' description='Visualization of implants and bone model will aid in implant planning in Web Planner. Figma concepts based on formative studies will drive the final arrangement of information. On a higher level following things needs to be considered - \n\n# 3D bone model - reconstructed 3D bone model from VOLT ( examples - both pelvis (x2), and femur (x2), Femur canal (operative side), Condyles (x2))\n# 3D Implant model - Imported from IDB. Mostly solid, different color for each type of component for easy differentiations\n# 3D model view options - Ability to zoom, pan, rotate 360 degrees. Some pre-defined views such as Anterior/posterior, medial/lateral, superior inferior. \n# 3D model Opacity/Transparency - Default transparency for each components and ability to change transparency in the range of complete opaque to complete transparent.\n# 2D representation of 3D models (used for Implant placement) - Showing the cross-section/outline of 3D models in a specific frame across the depth of 3D models in respective reference plane (coronal/sagittal/transverse). Model can be scrolled to pre-defined slice thickness to view a specific slice. Any landmarks, for example COR are projected through out the slides.\n# 2D model view options - Allow user to zoom, pan.\n# 2D Xray view - Option to show Xray or DRR if provided by Visionaire Engineer’s plan only for visualization, no processing.\n# Ability to expand/shrink screen sizes during implant planning.\n\n\n\nConsider compatibility with devices to accommodates commonly used screen sizes and resolution. \n\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported browsers - Latest versions by Dec 2023 - Chrome, Edge, Safari, firefox{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported screes for interaction - tablet, laptop, desktop ==> ~10”, 14”, 24” screens{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported screens only for display ~ 32”, 50” 70”{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported view - Landscape{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported user interfaces ==> touch screen, laptop touchpad + keys, mouse + keyboard{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported resolution - Fine as described SOW (1920x1080, 1440x900, 1366x768, 768×1024){color}\n\n{color:#ff5630}For no-compatible or non-supported situations – {color}{color:#ff5630}*Warning*{color}{color:#ff5630} about it but let user use the app at risk. It is acceptable to have non-optimal interaction or visual for non supported situations. {color}\n\nExample-\n\n!image-20230619-153653.png|width=1643,height=859!\n\nMore example screens attached.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:07,947 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48505 (CSTEST-607): summary='User Profile and Credentialing- Surgeon/Tech' description="{color:#ff5630}*Only consider the authentication on Web Planner based on authentication on VCM portal.*{color}\n\nOnce user already logs in VCM portal, Web planner authenticates user without asking to log in again. \n\n\n\n{color:#ff5630}*Most likely the front end will be implemented by Visionaire portal.*{color}\n\nUser will only have to go through login/authentication process once per session for accessing the portal/plan.\n\nMost likely, the front interface will be implemented on an existing Visionaire platform hence the web planner will not have any login/credentialing interface page for the user. However, in the background, Web portal needs to ensure that only authorized users on Visionaire platform are allowed the access of Web portal. \n\nWeb Portal also needs to implement safe timeout/log out. The details associated with this function will be determined after risk assessment.\n\n\n\nDetermine the types of users who will get access to the web portal and level of privileges. Likely users of the Web portal are - Surgeon, SN Rep, SN Visionaire Engineer.\n\n\n\nFollowing functions are likely to be available on Visionaire portal. Mentioned only for reference here -\n\nAbility for the user to view currently scheduled cases.\n\nAbility for the user to rearrange cases as pert the scheduled date, patient's first name and last name, etc..  \n\nAbility for the user to view archived or canceled cases and rearrange them\n\nUsers - Surgeons, Scheduler, SN Rep" issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:07,948 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48506 (CSTEST-606): summary='Communication-Import/Export with VCM Cloud' description='This feature describes the underline communication and import/export capability of the Web planner between different systems/databases.\n\nConsider encryption/decryption based on compliance needs.\n\n\n\n2 copies of plan in VCM cloud- \n\n* Copy 1  - VOLT version of the plan\n* Copy 2 - Start with VOLT copy, and override with surgeon changes\n\n\n\nFor each case - Web planner needs to import appropriate parameters from their respective locations (Microsoft 360 Dynamics/ Cumulous/ Visionaire) as defined in ICD.\n\n* Surface files - Patient bone/ generic bone, implants  - Visuals and measurements (could be .bj, .stl, or .wrl files)\n* Coordinates - Pelvic coordinates, Femur coordinates, reference planes APP/Functional, respective implant to bone coordinates, femur antitorsion, combined version\n* Measurements - Measurements calculated by VOLT engineer - SPM classification, Pelvic tilt, femur antitorsion, combined version, leg length/offset\n* Meta data - patient info, surgeon info, implant parameters, etc.\n* Images - Some specific images provided by VOLT plan\n* {color:#ff5630}Xray/DRR - If Xray (DRR) provide by Volt Plan{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Notes - Any notes from Engineer/Surgeon{color}\n\nFor each case Web planner needs to export appropriate parameters to their respective locations (Microsoft 360 Dynamics/ Cumulous/ Visionaire) as defined in ICD.\n\n* Surface files - Patient bone/ generic bone, implants  - Visuals and measurements\n* Coordinates - Pelvic coordinates, Femur coordinates, reference planes APP/Functional, respective implant to bone coordinates, \n* Measurements - Measurements values - SPM classification, Pelvic tilt, femur antitorsion, combined version, leg length/offset\n* Meta data - patient info, surgeon info, implant parameters, etc.\n* Images - Some specific images as part of the workflow or upon surgeon request\n* {color:#ff5630}Notes - Any notes from Engineer/Surgeon{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Xray/DRR - If Xray (DRR) provide by Volt Plan{color}\n* Report files - files such as finalized plan reports in formats which can be either printed or visualized in CORI Hip 7 - i.e. DICOM viewer compatible \n\n\n\nIdentify appropriate database locations for the category of data and define detailed data flow to and from various system components as part of ICD definition. \n\nDefine data types for each category after discussion with development team. \n\n\n\nInitial Data flow diagram - \n\n!image-20230511-182027.png|width=1243,height=974!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
