2026-07-21 00:03:07,974 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48202 (CSTEST-575): summary='RI Insights - Pre-Op Planning - Post-Operative Use of Data' description='{color:#ff5630}*User Facing text needs to align with final product naming and terminology.*{color}\n\n*LOGGING NEEDS (Navio Logs)*\nAdd information to log file that denotes case as image-based \n\n\n*SURGEON FACING RI.INSIGHTS NEEDS* *(including casedata.json)*\nAssumption: CORI team will create UKA casedata.json so that UKA data can be displayed in RI.INSIGHTS at the point in time when RI.INSIGHTS enables UKA case data display\n\n1) ”Behind-the-scenes” checkbox/filter to sort image-based outcomes (filter on planning averages)\n_Note: messaging should not indicate that IF is more or less accurate than IB and vice versa, implementation should not lead to comparisons between IF/IB outcomes_\n\n2) Add tag for image-based case in TKA/UKA casedata.json (presence of data in field (data = Visionaire case ID will indicate image-based case)\n\n3) Add tag for SPP in TKA casedata.json (helps us understand how impactful SPP is in terms of time spent in planning)\n\n4) Change status of plan based on Visionaire Case ID\n\n\n*CORI/NSYNC STORAGE NEEDS*\nAssumption(s): 1) no storage concerns on CORI/NSYNC, 2) Visionaire expiration data: 6 months from date of imaging\n\nAfter 6 months, do we 1) prevent users from using data outright or 2) do we need to notify users about expiration? Need to understand patient risk associated with these options. 5/10: leading option = #2' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:07,974 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48203 (CSTEST-574): summary='Pre-Op Planning - Use of Pre-Op Planning Data in Planning State' description='Add functionality to enable population of a Visionaire pre-operatively generated plan on CORI, in place of the current CORI initial plan that is generated in RI.KNEE Planning states when an image-based case workflow is initiated.\n\nFemur and tibia components, their sizes, and their pre-operatively planned positions should populate in the intraoperative implant planning states as the initial plan. Additionally, the patient’s 3D anatomical models should be displayed with their orientations/positions relative to the pre-operatively planned implant positions maintained from pre-operative planning. Importation of the above-mentioned items and maintenance of their pre-operatively planned relationships to one another should be driven by Registration (CORI-568) and carried into the implant planning states.  \n\nWhen considering the same patient, Visionaire pre-operatively planned implant positions will differ from CORI’s initial planned implant positions for several reasons (see link to slide deck under Technical Review section). Various methods for rectifying these differences have been outlined. Additional cross-functional team investigation, definition, and analysis is required to select a leading method ahead of development.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
