2026-07-21 00:03:08,020 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48349 (CSTEST-528): summary='Save all force values associated with collected gaps' description='Save force values associated with gap calculations in Pre-Op and Post-Op gap assessment screens. Need to explore whether this should replace the force setting value that is being saved currently or add to current data logs.\n\n*Need for collecting this data*: The Tensioner device is a new product out in the field and it has 3 force thresholds for recommended use in the field. The idea behind collecting this data is to understand how the joint space behaves outside of these force regions since the regions come out of calculations from usability etc and not entirely from the clinical understanding of joint laxity \n\n*What is to be collected*: Collect all force values that are associated with each transform when the trackers are visible. Create a threshold from when to start collecting this force to avoid collecting dead band force ( Focus on this if space the file is occupying on the disc is a concern) . Additionally add time stamps to collate the data\n\n*What is currently collected*: 1.7 software already captures all gap collections in sequential order (this includes rejected gaps and accepted gaps). The force bucket associated with every bin of gap data is saved in the gap files (rejected and accepted) for every collection.\n\n*Other considerations*: \n\n* Find creative ways to reduce the data collected. Options:\n** Compare transforms and data and save to disk only if they are different\n** Decide on a minimum force threshold to begin collecting data\n** Add a file size limit\n* Save to disk only during state transition to not impact the performance of the state by constantly writing to file\n* Run latency test before and after the feature is implemented to ensure the performance has not been affected\n* Store ALL planning data as well to recreate the scenarios in post processing. Save planning data along with state transition so that if plan changes , the gap state will reflect the new plan\n* Data should be compressed to avoid blowing up the size of a case on CORI\n* Compress data at the end of a session. If case is resumed , create a new compression at the end of that session\n* *Post processing of collected data is NOT included in this story.* Post processing data should consider the insertion of the Tensioner into the joint space affecting the gaps. This will not be related to application of force since the insertion will happen first before the handle is squeezed. Analyze and identify data pattern to recognize Tensioner insertion\n* Save current implant plan (implant selected, position, thickness etc.)\n\n\n\n{color:#6554c0}Dev Estimate (if done in Pittsburgh with one developer): 4 sprints{color}\n\n* {color:#6554c0}Includes unit testing/testing of data compression or find something off the shelf (add to SOUP). {color}\n* {color:#6554c0}Includes latency regression tests/analysis.{color}\n\n{color:#6554c0}Test estimate (if done in Pittsburgh with 1 tester): 5 sprints{color}\n\n* {color:#6554c0}Need to assess if the current Instron fixture can be used for this. {color}\n* {color:#6554c0}Need to assess validation of BIOS clock{color}\n* {color:#6554c0}This includes regression testing as well as testing of this new feature.{color}\n** {color:#6554c0}TP1426, 1431, and 10050321 (might need to update list){color}\n\n\n\n{color:#6554c0}Dev Estimate (if {color}{color:#6554c0}+not done in Pittsburgh with guidance from one Pittsburgh developer+{color}{color:#6554c0}): 6 sprints{color}\n\n{color:#6554c0}Test estimate (if {color}{color:#6554c0}+not done in Pittsburgh+{color}{color:#6554c0}): No instron in Pune{color}' issueType='Epic' status='Triage' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,021 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48245 (CSTEST-527): summary='Connected CORI: CyberSecurity Improvements on CORI' description='|Jira project|number|Description|\n| | | |\n|Optimus|1342|Create bbt-admin credentials that are unique to each device|\n|Optimus|1343|Create BIOS passwords that are unique to each device|\n|Optimus|1465|Disable WiFi in BIOS|\n|Optimus|1330|Define encryption of thumb drives|\n|Optimus|1311|Remove unnecessary USB keyboard driver support from OS|\n|Optimus|1312|Remove support for all unused USB connection modes|\n|Optimus|1313|Limit the specific USB drives that are allowed to be used|\n|Optimus|1402|Restrict "bluebelt" account privileges|\n|Optimus|1403|Restrict "bbt-admin" and "root" account privileges|\n|Optimus|1308|Evaluate hard drive encryption|\n|Optimus|1332|Ensure IDB and Language pack updates can be handled by encryption scheme|\n|Optimus|2936|Weak authentication parameters|\n|Optimus|2937|Disable or extremely limit RLT BLE radio/functionality|\n|Optimus|2938|Integrity check to validate firmware during manufacturing process|\n|Optimus|2939|Add checksums to mitigate buffer overflow vulnerabilities|\n|Optimus|2940|Encrypt session during processing to ensure protocol is encrypted|\n|Optimus|1309|Evaluate Removal of Hot Key Functionality to prevent terminal access|\n|Optimus|1318|Implement Hard Drive Encryption|\n|Optimus|1344|Update Ubuntu OS version|\n|Optimus|1405|Limit the exposed network services to the minimum required|\n|Optimus|1406|Upgrade Linux Kernel|\n|Optimus|1407|Implement TCU Firmware/Code Authentication|\n|Optimus|1408|Implement PMB Firmware/Code Authentication|\n|Optimus|1409|Log server authentication of the source of network connections|\n|Optimus|1410|Log server should refrain from creating files with a name provided by a client|\n|Optimus|1411|Mask the user\'s PIN on the New Surgeon/Change Surgeon screen|\n|Optimus|1412|Remove hardcoded encryption keys from source code|' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,021 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48246 (CSTEST-526): summary='Integrate with connected CORI' description='The CORI system is being enhanced to have network connectivity and connect to the cloud to upload data and remove the need for USB transfers. The CORI system will be have the capability to upload data as soon as case is completed for a surgeon. The CORI system will also have the ability to do a bulk upload of cases for a selected surgeon.\n\nCumulus will become the destination for the data to be uploaded. The Cumulus system will support a secure connection between the devices to accept case and log files that will be uploaded from multiple systems from across the globe.\n\nOnce the data is uploaded the system will parse the data, identify valid cases, and assign data owners for RI.Insights app to visualize the cases once available.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,021 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48247 (CSTEST-525): summary='Tensioner Data on Cumulus' description='Tensioner is being released to the market has an enhancement to TKA procedures. Gaps will be collected using the new accessory. Data collected from these surgeries will be valuable to the surgeons and SN.\n\nThe surgeons would like to know the force that was used to gather the graphs across all bins and also overlay data over manual gap collection to better compare two approaches. Recorded data is target bucket not the raw data. The surgeon would benefit from understanding a trend of force applied for certain deformity ranges. They would also benefit from understanding the outcomes for tensioned vs manual gap collection.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,023 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48248 (CSTEST-524): summary='Improve functionality of Cori soft shutdown slider' description="Created from bug 1701.  Description from Jeremy:\n\nThere's two separate issues here:\n\n\xa01. It's easy for the slider control to lose track of progress.\n\n\xa0It is a known issue that the circle on the slider control resets if you release your finger or touch anywhere outside of the slider's interaction zone, but I don't know if users are aware that the state logic does not check for a CONTINUOUS slide gesture. Instead, it is only checking for an interaction on the far right of the slider. The slider control will always snap the slider to your current interaction point - so if you touched the slider in the middle, the circle will automatically be redrawn in the middle of the slider control.\n\n\xa0Even if the slider loses track of your progress, you can keep sliding along the control until you notice the circle snapping back to the location of your finger.\n\n\xa0This interaction was confirmed on DV03. I started dragging my finger on the left side of the slider, then moved it slightly above the slider. The circle followed my finger until I moved it above the slider, then it snapped to the left side of the slider. I then dragged my finger back down to the slider, and the circle snapped back to the current location of my finger.\n\n\xa0So, I was not able to observe DV03 having an issue with shutting down due to the gesture control for the shutdown slider. At the same time, I could understand that a user who was not familiar with how the slider works would have an issue if they continued to swipe the screen from the left every time it reset. This leads into the next issue.\n\n\xa02. The power-off slider has a frustratingly-narrow interaction zone.\n\n\xa0This one is slightly harder to address. Talking with Natalie about our options, it looks like we are extremely limited by our choice of hardware - the 4D Systems display. 4D Systems developed a proprietary DIABLO16 graphics controller based around a virtual processor, which is optimized to execute compiled code written in a proprietary high-level language (4DGL). In short, we're tied to the 4D Systems IDE, build process, and particular interactions regarding the display.\n\n\xa0If we use the current slider control, an easy solution would involve increasing the width of the slider control (including the orange bar) to account for the increased interaction zone. This would look different from the other sliders, so we may need Marketing's input before proceeding with this option.\n\n\xa0Alternatively, Natalie believes we can develop a new slider control, but we would need to research how the other slider control was developed and make the adjustments accordingly. It may also involve replacing the volume and irrigation slider controls to make sure that all three look the same. It's certainly not a trivial task, but we don't know how much effort will be involved just yet." issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
