2026-07-21 00:03:08,027 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48254 (CSTEST-509): summary='ri.OS Platform Creation' description='RI.OS software architecture is meant to replace the current CORI software architecture, in order to make application development, testing, and deployment faster, easier, and less complex. Without proper upkeep, software typically takes on technical debt and degrades, making it more difficult over time to modify or even create new components. Our goal is to introduce a new architecture, and provide the tools to use that architecture, in order to optimize our application development in all the ways that matter to us. In short, \n\nA key consideration in developing RI.OS is that it must be possible to migrate from the current architecture to RI.OS in an incremental fashion.\n\nThe updates to the TKA application will begin the process of migrating CORI software applications to the new architecture.' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
