2026-07-21 00:03:08,061 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48525 (CSTEST-460): summary='Kensci-Global Deployments to Lumino Geographies' description='Cumulus V2 is tasked with deploying our current product into a number of OUS regions to support our existing CORI and RI.INSIGHTS footprint. Users from the specified regions will need access to their data and as a project team we must ensure that their data is located in regions that comply with local regulatory and data residency standards.\n\nThis ticket encompasses the work required from the Cumulus team to build and deploy the application and databases to the appropriate Lumino-supported geographies.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,068 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48526 (CSTEST-459): summary='ActiveArm: Disposable Blade for Saw End Effector' description='When using a https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412 to complete a  https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-457 a sterile packed disposable blade will be required to make the bone cuts\n\nThe final COGS target for the saw blade (including sterilization and packaging) is $50.  This will make the COGS of the blade equivalent to the CORI bur.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,069 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48527 (CSTEST-458): summary='Kensci-Backend Global Data Segmentation' description='This epic supports the KenSci Sync up to support ensuring the Cumulus application has ability to support globalized customers where users can be supported everywhere that KenSci currently supports.\n\nThis includes ensuring we have hosting and architecture that allows segmentation of the data into the following buckets:\n\n* Individual User - Cases that apply to the surgeon\n* Customer group of users - groups of users under the same customer\n* Country - Cases that originate from the same country\n* Regional - Cases that are in groups of countries (APAC, EMEA, LATAM, North America)\n\nCreate the backend and master authorizations for access to each level of data' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,070 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48528 (CSTEST-457): summary='ActiveArm: TKA Saw Workflow' description='The active arm should be able to support a bone preparation workflow where a saw[https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412|smart-link]  is automatically positioned[https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-393|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-393|smart-link]  to each femur and tibia cutting plane used in Smith + Nephew Total Knee Replacements and then used to execute each cut through the surgeon’s typical incision without the need for a cutting guide, pins or additional instrumentation\n\nThe cuts should be able to be completed in any order that the user prefers.  The users preference of cut order should be able to be saved and selected ahead of time. [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-465|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-465|smart-link] \n\nIn order to ensure a successful procedure it is important that the soft tissue structures of the knee are protected.  This can be accomplished through a combination of [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-396|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-396|smart-link] and [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-456|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-456|smart-link] \n\nThe time required to complete the cuts should be the same or less than completing a manual procedure.  The time requirement could be tested by completing a cadaveric time trial where a surgeon prepares 1 leg of the same specimen with the arm and 1 leg of the same specimen with manual instruments.\n\nThe following implants should be supported:\n\n* JOURNEY 2 CR and BCS\n* JOURNEY 2 CR Porous, JOURNEY 2 BCS Porous\n* LEGION CR and PS (Both Standard and Narrow)\n* LEGION CR Porous, LEGION PS Porous (Both Standard and Narrow)\n* GENESIS II CR and PS\n* ANTHEM CR and PS (Both Standard and Narrow)\n* Universal Cemented and CONCELOC baseplate\n\nConstraints:\n\n# Does not require additional instrumentation' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,070 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48529 (CSTEST-456): summary='ActiveArm Saw End Effector Tactile Feedback During Cutting' description='When using a saw end effector [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412|smart-link] with the active arm both visibility and tactile feedback within the knee are limited compared to using a saw during a manual procedure. \n\nIn addition to [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-396|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-396|smart-link] surgeons want to be able to have tactile feedback when the completing saw cuts for a total knee replacement\n\nUsability labs completed in 2021 utilized a joystick in order to control the robotic arm.  Feedback from these labs all expressed a concern that the surgeons felt too “disconnected” from the cutting tool.\n\nSpecific anatomical structures where additional tactile feedback is desired include include:\n\n* Transitions from cancellous to cortical bone \n* Popliteal Artery\n* Patellar Tendon\n* MCL\n* LCL\n* PCL\n* ACL' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,071 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48282 (CSTEST-455): summary='Update CORI Operating System from Ubuntu 16' description='The current version of the CORI Ubuntu 16.04 operating system  is end of life.   We need to define the plan forward on how to upgrade the OS to a supported version.   \n\nThere is at least one customer that we have aggreged through a letter to ensure we are on a supported version of an Operating system by 2023.\n\n========================\n\n*Scope of Work*\n\n* Migrate CORI 2.0 baseline code to Ubuntu v22.0.4\n* Upgrade CORI Connectivity features (IRIS) baseline to Ubuntu 22.04\n* SOUP documentation of all tools/3rd party libraries which need upgrade to Ubuntu 22.04 to include following information\n** Name of the Software\n** The Software developer/provider\n** Version number\n** Build number, if available\n** Version release notes, if available\n** List of known bugs, if available\n* Dry Run Verification of CORI 2.1, post integration of Defect fixes, CORI Connectivity features and Ubuntu 22.04 upgrade on CORI 2.0' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,071 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48283 (CSTEST-454): summary='Long Attachments Getting Stuck On Handpiece' description='An increasing number of complaints are being submitted (Qty. 16 in November(updated Nov 22) and 8 in October, see attachment),  where the user is unable to disconnect the long attachment from the handpiece after completing a CORI case.  When this happens the long attachment, handpiece tracker and handpiece must be replaced because they are unable to be separating in the field.  \n\nThis is likely due to a pin in the long attachment backing out in most cases.  \n\nThis ticket is requesting 2 actions:\n\n# Recommendation and supporting materials provided to the field that can mitigate this issue in the near term and reduce the pressure on handpiece inventory (see business case section).  This could be a recommendation to monitor the component and remove it from use prior to it getting stuck, limiting long attachment use to X number of uses, or similar instructions that would prevent the loss of a handpiece\n# Design change or manufacturing process improvement to prevent this failure mode from occurring\n\n\n\n[^report1637762267161.xls]\n\n \nSee below complaints for examples:\nCASE-2020-00011493\nCASE-2020-00013123\nCASE-2020-00014008\nCASE-2020-00015681\nCASE-2020-00017747\nCASE-2020-00017837\nCASE-2020-00018541\nCASE-2020-00018541\nCASE-2020-00018541\nCASE-2020-00018508\nCASE-2020-00018854\nCASE-2020-00021762\nCASE-2020-00033328\nCASE-2020-00034880\nCASE-2020-00035608\nCASE-2021-00037543\nCASE-2021-00041501\nCASE-2021-00042224\nCASE-2021-00042978\nCASE-2021-00044583\nCASE-2021-00044827\nCASE-2021-00047294\nCASE-2021-00047929\nCASE-2021-00049328\nCASE-2021-00049321\nCASE-2021-00050861\nCASE-2021-00052707\nCASE-2021-00052107\nCASE-2021-00053599\nCASE-2021-00057177\nCASE-2021-00062516\nCASE-2021-00065914\nCASE-2021-00068947\nCASE-2021-00069009\nCASE-2021-00072802\nCASE-2021-00074008\nCASE-2021-00074230\nCASE-2021-00075038\nCASE-2021-00075265\nCASE-2021-00075778\nCASE-2021-00076948\nCASE-2021-00076959\nCASE-2021-00077480\nCASE-2021-00077305\nCASE-2021-00077845\nCASE-2021-00078283\nCASE-2021-00079400\nCASE-2021-00079637\nCASE-2021-00080415\nCASE-2021-00080064\nCASE-2021-00079861\nCASE-2021-00079832\nCASE-2021-00080888\nCASE-2021-00080849\nCASE-2021-00080427\nCASE-2021-00080455\nCASE-2021-00080851\nCASE-2021-00080856\nCASE-2021-00080722\nCASE-2021-00081538\nCASE-2021-00081426\nCASE-2021-00081455\nCASE-2021-00082209' issueType='Epic' status='Implementing' parent=None
