2026-07-21 00:03:08,104 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48304 (CSTEST-420): summary='Next Gen CORI Console' description='A new CORI console is needed in order to provide enhanced performance as well as support additional applications and new accessories\n\n*Application Support:* The next gen CORI Console should support all applications and software architectures that CORI currently supports as well as any applications that are planned to be supported prior to and after launch of the next gen CORI Console.   \n\n* TKA \n* UKA \n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-341|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-341|smart-link]\n* THA Nav \n* Robotic THA\n* Revision TKA software application \n* Robotic Revision THA\n*  [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-463|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-463|smart-link] \n* Robotic FAI\n* Robotic Shoulder\n* ACL\n\n*Accessory Support:* The next gen CORI Console should support all accessories that CORI currently supports as well as any accessories that are planned to be supported prior to or after launch of the next gen CORI Console.\n\n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-444|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-444|smart-link]\n*  [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-411|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-411|smart-link] \n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-383|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-383|smart-link] \n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-379|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-379|smart-link] \n* USB - C support\n* Wireless tablet support\n* Ability to charge wireless devices\n* Current CORI Handpiece\n* TBD - Sports\n\n*Flexible and Scalable Hardware:*  The next gen CORI Console should be designed so additional robotics and connectivity solutions can be added when they become available and current modules can be upgraded when needed.\n\n* Support multiple configurations including OR integration and the option to not use a cart\n* Camera mounted to boom\n* Communication and integration with other Smith and Nephew devices (ie. INTELLIO LYNC, LENS 4K, ect.) \n\nThe modules should be structured in a way that allows for simple logistics and distribution:\n\n* Base Module - contains hardware needed to provide existing CORI functionality\n* Expansion Module 1\n* Expansion Module 2\n* ect.\n\n*User Experience Improvements:*  The next generation CORI console should improve the user experience where possible.  Current drawbacks of the current CORI console include:\n\n* Touch screen slider is difficult to use\n* Robust bootup and shutdown process\n* Single button press bootup\n* Improved port availability (Additional ethernet ports, HDMI)\n* Front USB ports are too close together\n* Eliminate all dongles\n* Eliminate bone model loading time\n* Power loss prevention (less than 1 minute)\n\n*Image and Video Viewing:*  \n\n* Reliable external monitor support\n* 4K Video\n* High quality Image Display (ie. DICOM)\n* HDMI, DisplayPort, DVI, VGA, SDI ports\n* Support boom mounted monitors and AV systems\n\n*Connectivity and Data Storage:*\n\n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-370|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-370|smart-link] \n* Wireless data transfer to RI Insights\n* Ensure enough data storage to store data from all cases for 5 years\n* Preoperative Imaging solutions (CT and MRI) [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-384|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-384|smart-link] \n* PACS connectivity\n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-342|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-342|smart-link] \n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-452|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-452|smart-link] \n\n*Serviceability:*  \n\n* Remote Software Updates\n* Wireless Case data import and export \n* Keyboard and mouse support\n* In field hardware serviceability\n\n*Internationalization:*  The new console should be designed so that CORI can be sold in top performing markets where CORI is available or planned to be available prior to the launch of the next gen CORI Console.  Learnings from the current CORI console should be considered and implemented in the next gen Console:\n\n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-483|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-483|smart-link] \n* Robust EMC in order to avoid flickering when used in different markets (ie. 120v and 220v)\n* SKU management (supply and regulatory registration considerations)\n\n*COGS:*  The base configuration should have equivalent COGS as the current CORI console ($8000)\n\n*Transportation and Shipping:*' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,105 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48534 (CSTEST-419): summary='ActiveArm: Minimize Reusable Instruments for TKA' description='Instruments required for use with an Active Arm procedure need to be provided in a sterilization tray that integrates into the CORI tray system and minimizes the number of trays required for a CORI procedure (this includes both CORI and manual knee system instruments).  \n\nActive Arm Specific Instruments may include the following:\n\n* End Effector (ie. saw, drill, or cut guide)\n* End Effector Tracker\n* End effector interface\n\nCORI Instruments that may be required for an active arm TKA procedure may include:\n\n* Point Probe\n* Femur and Tibia Trackers\n* Tracker attachment hardware\n\nManual Knee System Instruments that may be required for an active arm TKA procedure may include:\n\n* Trial Implants\n* Impactors and finishing instruments' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,106 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48535 (CSTEST-418): summary='ActiveArm: Disposable Sterile Drape' description='The active arm contains both non-sterile hardware and instruments that can be sterilized.  The non-sterile hardware is required to be in the sterile field when in use.  In order to use the arm it must be covered in sterile disposable drape.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,106 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48536 (CSTEST-417): summary='ActiveArm: Leg Stabilization' description='A leg stabilization method is not desired but may be required in order to ensure cut accuracy.  If a leg stabilization device is required for technical reasons then a solution should consider the following:\n\n# Impact to surgical workfllow - Ease of assembly and restrictions to other steps (ie. hip center)\n# Minimize additional cost - both COGS and sterilization' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,107 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48537 (CSTEST-415): summary='ActiveArm: Arm Cart' description='A mobile, compact and lightweight cart is needed to support the Active Arm during use as well as facilitate transportation throughout the hospital.  The footprint of the arm should be minimized so it does not interfere with the surgery.  \n\n*Non Sterile Setup* - The system should guide the user through required setup steps and calibrations.  Where possible, the UI should clearly show the user what they need to do.  A non-sterile person should be able to complete as many of the setup tasks as possible\n\n*Sterile Setup -* The cart should help facilitate the sterile draping and sterile instrument attachment process\n\n*Operation* - During use the arm cart should not impede the operative flow of the surgeon, PA or scrub tech\n\n*Removal from sterile field* - The arm should be able to be removed from the sterile field after its use is finished  in order to get it out of the way and prepare it for another surgery.\n\n*Storage* - When not in use the combined footprint of the Arm Cart and the CORI Cart should be minimized in order to take up less space in a hospital closet or hallway.  Both carts should look like they belong together and ideally nest in order to minimize footprint.  A customized dust cover is desirable\n\n*Transport within hospital* - A single person should be able to move the cart between operating rooms, hallways and storage closets within a hospital.  This includes going through standard doorways and elevators\n\n*Shipping* - Shippable components should be below the maximum allowable size and weight of conventional shipping carriers (ie. Fedex and UPS).  Because the overall weight of the cart is likely to exceed the maximum weight, a modular design is desired\n\n* The Active arm component is most likely to be required to be returned to a service center and therefore should be easily detachable from the support structure.  \n* Electronics - It is likely that additional weight will be required for stability of the arm during operation.  Therefore, where possible, system electronics (ie. communications gateways, e-stop, manipulator electronics, UPS, transformer ect.) should be moved into the cart.  Electronics that are likely to require service should be modular and able to be removed from the support structure\n* Support Structure and weight - Contains components that are field serviceable (ie. casters, cables, ect.)' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,107 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48538 (CSTEST-414): summary='ActiveArm: End Effector - Cut Guide' description='This a physical part to support [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-410|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-410|smart-link] \n\nThe cutting guide needs to be able to be attached and detached from the robotic arm during system setup.  \n\nThe cutting guide should not be required to be pinned to the bone or separated from the arm in order to make each cut.  If additional stability is needed, a portion of the cutting guide could contact the bone.  The same cutting guide should be used to make all of the cuts in order to minimize instrumentation and maximize efficiency.\n\n*Note:  Some cuts are more narrow than others (ie. the medial and lateral posterior cuts).  It may be beneficial the have multiple slots within the same guide to prepare wide (ie. distal cut) and narrow cuts (ie. posterior)\n\nThe cutting guide should integrate into the overall CORI tray system[https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-419|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-419|smart-link]' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,108 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48539 (CSTEST-412): summary='ActiveArm: End Effector - Saw' description='This is an electromechanical device that the [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-411|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-411|smart-link] will use to complete the [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-457|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-457|smart-link] \n\n*Setup*\n\nThe saw should be a single unit that does not require assembly by the scrub tech after removing it from the instrumentation tray.\n\nA [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-459|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-459|smart-link] will need to be connected to the saw prior to being used.  It is desirable for this task to be completed by the scrub tech on the back table prior to the patient or arm being in their final position to streamline intraoperative workflow\n\nThe saw should be able to be connected to the [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-415|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-415|smart-link] quickly and without using any tools.  If calibrations are required then they should be able to be completed prior to the arm or patient being placed in their final position\n\n*Use During Bone Removal*\n\nThe saw will be positioned along each cutting plane using [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-393|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-393|smart-link] and the surgeon will activate the cutting tool prior to completing each cut.  While making each cut the surgeon should be able to ergonomically control the position of the saw and feel the progress of the cuts through the bone [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-456|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-456|smart-link] \n\n*Sterilization and Processing* \n\nThe saw end effector will need to be sterilized between uses as part of the instrumentation tray [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-419|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-419|smart-link] .  It should be able to be processed using the same autoclave, autowash and disinfection cycles that are available for the CORI instrumentation.  Where possible, special cleaning instructions should be avoided.\n\n*Service*\n\nIf regular maintenance is required then it should be able to be completed onsite and no more frequent than once a year.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,108 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48305 (CSTEST-411): summary='Active Arm Platform' description='Develop an active robotic arm platform that can be used as an additional bone preparation accessory to the CORI Surgical System.  \n\nThe active robotic arm should be a flexible platform that can utilize different tools to perform specific tasks required for the target procedure.  \n\nThe active arm may need to support the following end effectors as well as future end effectors [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-412|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-414|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-414|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-413|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-413|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-402|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-402|smart-link][https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-403|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-403|smart-link]  \n\nIn order to provide stability, maneuverability and house electrical components the arm will be mounted on a  mobile cart [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-415|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-415|smart-link] .  The cart in combination with the robotic arm should provide enough stability and reach in order to use end effectors to complete multiple surgical procedures including [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-457|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-457|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-410|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-410|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-469|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-469|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-470|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-470|smart-link] \n\nThe arm should have multiple control modes that can be used in combination with one another to complete surgical workflows [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-471|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-471|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-406|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-406|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-456|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-456|smart-link] [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-398|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-398|smart-link] \n\nWhen completing a surgery the robotic arm should be able to maintain a cutting plane or trajectory in response to movement of the bone [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-468|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-468|smart-link]' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,110 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48540 (CSTEST-410): summary='ActiveArm: TKA Cut Guide Workflow' description='The active arm should be able to support a bone preparation workflow where a cutting guide is automatically positioned to each femur and tibia cutting plane used in Smith + Nephew Total Knee Replacements.\n\nAfter the cutting guide is positioned to the plane, active compensation should keep the cutting guide on the plane.\n\nThe cutting guide should not be required to be pinned to the bone or separated from the arm in order to make each cut.  If additional stability is needed, a portion of the cutting guide could contact the bone.\n\nThe same cutting guide should be used to make all of the cuts in order to minimize instrumentation and maximize efficiency.\n\nThe cuts should be able to be completed in any order that the user prefers.  The users preference of cut order should be able to be saved and selected ahead of time.\n\nThe time required to complete the cuts should be the same or less than completing a manual procedure.  The time requirement could be tested by completing a cadaveric time trial where a surgeon prepares 1 leg of the same specimen with the arm and 1 leg of the same specimen with manual instruments.\n\nThe following implants should be supported:\n\n* JOURNEY 2 CR and BCS\n* JOURNEY 2 CR Porous, JOURNEY 2 BCS Porous\n* LEGION CR and PS (Both Standard and Narrow)\n* LEGION CR Porous, LEGION PS Porous (Both Standard and Narrow)\n* GENESIS II CR and PS\n* ANTHEM CR and PS (Both Standard and Narrow)\n* Universal Cemented and CONCELOC baseplate\n\n\n\nConstraints:\n\n# Cut Guide shall be pinless\n# A single cut guide shall be used for 1 procedure\n\nAssumptions:' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
