2026-07-21 00:03:08,123 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48329 (CSTEST-355): summary='Addition of IR and ER to Axis Definition Screen' description='Surgeons want to know if they are defining their femur and/or tibia axes in an externally or internally rotated manner relative to the CORI defined PCA. \n\nTo facilitate this request, internal rotation or external rotation (IR/ER) labels should be added to any state where we can change axis definition (femur and tibia).\n\n\n* If a surgeon is defining this axis as 0 degrees, the state shall simply indicate "0°" like it does today. \n* If the axis is being defined at a value other than 0, the on-screen text shall indicate "#° IE" or "#° IR" relative to the PCA. \n\n\n\n!image-20250115-145308.png|width=964,height=536,alt="image-20250115-145308.png"!\n\n\n\n!image-20250115-145118.png|width=758,height=427,alt="image-20250115-145118.png"!' issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,124 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48330 (CSTEST-354): summary='Updates to Implant Parameter Values on Planning and Case Review Screens' description='This feature has two goals:\n\n# Provide consistency among depcition (integer or decimal) of resection. angulation, numeric values on planning and case review screens. \n## Update visuals on planning and case review screens to reflect .5mm increments (log files can maintain raw data)\n# Provide customization for visualization of implant resections to decrease learning curve of surgeons\n## Surgeon selection for resections by component (i.e. what we have today - femur and tibia resections independently) \n## Surgeon selection for combined resection depth (femur and tibia resections combined)' issueType='Epic' status='Define' parent=None
