2026-07-21 00:03:08,146 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48567 (CSTEST-332): summary='Planning: Utilization of Preference in Planning as Initial Placement' description='Implementation of using information set from surgeon profile as initial starting position for implant components. \n\nUse case of reverting back to CORI plan or preferred plan needed - ability to reset F/T to either preferred plan or CORI plan\n\n* There will be a button to reset the preferred plan and a button to reset to Cori default initial plan for both femur and tibia (4 buttons total, 2 newe for preferred planning reset)\n\nThe decision to use the SDIP plan vs the Cori default initial plan will be made at the surgeon planning portal in launcher.  If there is an initial plan saved for the deformity bucket that the patient falls within then Cori will apply that, otherwise use the Cori initial default plan.  No other ‘apply SDIP’ in planning or surgeon preferences is necessary.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,146 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48344 (CSTEST-331): summary='Planning: Autopopulate Averages' description='Creating an initial plan based on previous plans or preferences created by that surgeon based on averages, \n\nPlease see attached presentation for description of prototyped flow and parameters of surgeon driven initial planning, including when and where averages are displayed and when auto-population occurs. \n\nCORI system should calculate averages based on segment of case data being analyzed and auto-populate in surgeon profile, per the attached.' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
