2026-07-21 00:03:08,148 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48568 (CSTEST-329): summary='Planning: Save Multiple preferences' description='Creating an initial plan based on previous plans or preferences created by that surgeon by:\n\n* Setting preferences in Surgeon Planning screen using reference files imported to the system, and\n* Updating preferences to match implant placement done in completed TKA case (at Case Review screen)  \n\nSurgeons should be able to save implant preferences for multiple deformities - set preferences/parameters for all deformity buckets. \n\nPlease see attached PPT.\n\nTo facilitate record tracking , an automatic screenshot should be taken about these preferences, in relation to the cases. and should be saved within the surgeon files. Ideally, preferences set should be exported with relevant cases in a human readable format. \n\n**Values should be able to be manipulated to the 0.5mm or 0.5 deg – This will match Combined Planning' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,148 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48346 (CSTEST-328): summary='Ability to set/change implant rotation points in TKA' description='Surgeons want the ability to change the point around an implant rotates in planning. \n\nAdditional surgeon preferences to be included (prior to and/or within planning) to optimize any adjustments after initial placement of the implant. \n\n* +Femur coronal view+ - Surgeon can intra-operatively (in planning) select/change the point about which the varus/valgus of the implant pivots \n** i.e. knee center, distal medial, distal lateral\n* +Tibia coronal view+ - Surgeon can intra-operatively (in planning) select/change the point about which the varus/valgus of the implant pivots\n** i.e. knee center, medial plateau, lateral plateau.\n* +Femur transverse view+ - Extension of Femoral Rotation Center selection - surgeon can intra-operatively (in planning) select/change the point about which the femur implant rotates \n** i.e. knee center, posterior medial, posterior lateral\n* +Tibia sagittal view+ - surgeon can intra-operatively (in planning) select/change the point about which tibia slope is pivoted. \n** i.e. anterior point, knee center\n\nThis feature shall be available in image-free and image-based workflows. Default behavior to be defined.  \n\nTo facilitate record tracking, the selected rotation points should be logged OR an automatic screenshot should be taken upon entry and exit of this state(s) and should be saved within the surgeon files. Ideally, preferences set should be exported with relevant cases in a human readable format.' issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,149 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48569 (CSTEST-327): summary='Planning: Surgeon Profile' description='Creating an initial plan based on previous plans or preferences created by that surgeon by:\n\n* Setting preferences in Surgeon Planning screen using reference files imported to the system, and\n* Updating preferences to match implant placement done in completed TKA case (at Case Review screen) \n\nGeneration surgeon profile button from “choose case” screen. Allows HCP to set/view planning preferences for various deformities. \n\nFrom this profile, the surgeon can set his/her preferences for specific implants and deformities and can choose to implement these preferences as their initial plan.  This feature can operate independently from Connected CORI features. \n\nTo facilitate record tracking, an automatic screenshot should be taken upon entry and exit of this state, and should be saved within the surgeon files. Preferences and references set should be exported with relevant cases where used, and with system log exports in a human readable format. \n\nImporting reference files:\n\nReference files created externally (outside the CORI system) will be imported and saved in the CORI system via a USB stick. A new import button will be added to the Admin Screen in Launcher to Import, View, and Delete reference files.\n\nAll imported reference files will be available for viewing and selection in the Surgeon Profile screen. On selection of a reference file in the  Surgeon Profile screen, reference values will be displayed in a format that differentiates it from the preferences being set with arrow buttons.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 00:03:08,149 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48347 (CSTEST-326): summary='Revision Indication Addition w/ technique on existing application' description='BBT document traceability to support and claim indication expansion for Revision Knee with current CORI TKA software. \n\nClinical feedback and currently utilized technique to be captured into a surgeon-authored document detailing steps. \n\n\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nNOTE: This does not replace clinical and market need for software features specifically for revision knee, as detailed in other epics on the Kanban board. \n{panel}' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
