2026-07-21 22:34:21,754 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48163 (CSTEST-678): summary='Multi Role per user profile' description='We need the ability to assign multiple roles to a single user profile. RAR user profile is for insights data upload and surgeon support, while sales rep role in NSYNC is created to suuport pre-op plans, for users who play both roles for an account we should provide access for those users to all pages for both roles.\n\nA user can play multiple roles in the Cumulus system. They could be both admin and customer service and RAR and Sale rep.\xa0Additional user roles are conditional to the first user role selected. If RAR is selected then only Sales rep is an additional option, the same works for Customer service and admin\xa0\n\n* If RAR is selected first, Sales Rep can be added.\n* If Sales Rep is selected first, RAR can be added.\n* If Admin is selected first, Customer service can be added.\n* If Customer service is selected first, Admin can be added.\xa0\n* Admin and Customer Service\n** Dashboard Changes: No changes\n** Page Options: Show pre-op plans page\n* RAR and Sales Rep.\n** Dashboard Changes: Add a new tab on the dashboard to show pre-op plan widgets- Customer and pending case count.\n\nPage Options: Show pre-op plans page on the left navigation screen.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,754 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48164 (CSTEST-677): summary='RI Insights ONLY - Pre-Op Planning - Post-Operative Use of Data' description='{color:#ff5630}*User Facing text needs to align with final product naming and terminology.*{color}\n\n*LOGGING NEEDS (Navio Logs)*\nAdd information to log file that denotes case as image-based \n\n\n*SURGEON FACING RI.INSIGHTS NEEDS* *(including casedata.json)*\nAssumption: CORI team will create UKA casedata.json so that UKA data can be displayed in RI.INSIGHTS at the point in time when RI.INSIGHTS enables UKA case data display\n\n1) ”Behind-the-scenes” checkbox/filter to sort image-based outcomes (filter on planning averages)\n_Note: messaging should not indicate that IF is more or less accurate than IB and vice versa, implementation should not lead to comparisons between IF/IB outcomes_\n\n2) Add tag for image-based case in TKA/UKA casedata.json (presence of data in field (data = Visionaire case ID will indicate image-based case)\n\n3) Add tag for SPP in TKA casedata.json (helps us understand how impactful SPP is in terms of time spent in planning)\n\n4) Change status of plan based on Visionaire Case ID\n\n\n*CORI/NSYNC STORAGE NEEDS*\nAssumption(s): 1) no storage concerns on CORI/NSYNC, 2) Visionaire expiration data: 6 months from date of imaging\n\nAfter 6 months, do we 1) prevent users from using data outright or 2) do we need to notify users about expiration? Need to understand patient risk associated with these options. 5/10: leading option = #2' issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
