2026-07-21 22:34:21,769 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48470 (CSTEST-651): summary='ADLs3- Preset motions' description='* As a Surgeon, I would like to know the impingement-free range of motion (ROM) in standard clinical maneuvers. \n* These tests are simple motions in just a single direction (e.g. flexion to impingement) or combinations of two motions (e.g. FLEX 90 + IR = flexion to 90 deg + internal rotation to impingement).\n* The preset motions are pre-defined and cannot be modified by the user. \n* The output of the preset motions is the ROM before impingement. For example, for the FLEX 90 + IR preset, a realistic output would be 90 deg of flexion + 32 deg of internal rotation. The preset output is calculated in the background by moving the femur along the preset direction and stopping when impingement occurs. \n* As I update the implant types/size or their placement, the preset output should update live. For example, if the flexion ROM is 121 deg and the user increases neck length, the flexion ROM might increase to 127 deg. \n* If the user clicks on a preset icon, the 3D model will show the motion of the femur along the motion trajectory, similar to the ADL simulations. The main difference is that the animation ends when impingement is detected and the 3D model is left in the final impinging position. \n\n!Capture (2b5d0a32-a057-4081-8d6a-3fca1556916c).JPG|width=25%!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,770 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48471 (CSTEST-650): summary='3D+2D Workflow Options' description='likely duplicate of [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-634|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-634]\n\n\n\nSurgeon will have the ability to interact with Web Plan - \n\nIn the absence of all the information available in the engineer plan, the Web planner will assumed predefine values. \n\nTypical 3D workflow scenarios to consider- \n\n|*Scenario*|*Input Images*|*Engineer Workflow Steps*|*Web Planning Workflow Steps*|\n|1|CT +\n2 lateral Xray|Engineer prepares the plan\n\n•Patient specific – PHI, Bones, Spinopelvic classification, Pelvic tilt\n•Surgeons specific – Implant selection and placements|Surgeon reviews/updates the plan, and generates report\n\n•Allowed to change - Spinopelvic classification, Pelvic tilt\n•Allowed to change - Implant parameters – type, size, placement\n•Generates reports - printable/digital|\n|2|CT +\nNo Lateral Xray|Engineer prepares the plan\n\n•Patient specific – PHI, Bones, *assumed normal Spinopelvic classification and 0 Pelvic tilt*\n•Surgeons specific – Implant selection and placements|Surgeon reviews/updates the plan, and generates report\n\n•Informed for *assumed Spinopelvic classification, and Pelvic tilt*|\n\n\n\nTypical 2D workflow scenarios to consider - \n\n|*Scenario*|*Input Images*|*Engineer Workflow Steps*|*Web Planning Workflow Steps*|\n|3|2 Lateral Xray|Engineer landmarks Xrays\n\n•Patient specific – PHI, Spinopelvic classification, Pelvic tilt\n•Surgeons specific – Implant selection|Surgeon reviews/updates the plan, and generates report\n\n•Informed for *assumed generic pelvic*\n•*NO - femur, bony impingement, leg L/O*\n•*Generic implant size, placement*\n•*Several implant selection/placement options with no impact on ADLs*|\n|4|No Image|No Engineer action\n\n•Patient specific – PHI\n•Surgeons specific – Implant selection|Surgeon reviews/updates the plan, and generates report\n\n•Informed for *assumed generic pelvic, SPM, and P. Tilt*\n•*NO - femur, bony impingement, leg L/O*\n•*Generic implant size, placement*\n•*Several implant selection/placement options with no impact on ADLs*\n•Could be a *training* tool/feature without patient specific profile|\n\nNice to have feature to review file -\n\n|*Scenario*|*Input Images*|*Engineer Workflow Steps*|*Web Planning Workflow Steps*|\n|5|AP Xray|No Engineer action|Option 1- No Web Planner Support.\n\nOption 2 – Web planner allows *upload* of static AP template file *only for visualization* from desktop/usb to review.|\n\n\n\n*General ideas for the workflow* - \n\n* Keep the workflow and user interactions for Ct-based and CT-free options similar.\n* Where appropriate, use risk mitigation by warning message or information about assumptions.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,770 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48472 (CSTEST-649): summary='Visionaire Engineer Training - Hip Procedure(s), Implants, and Planning' description='Training for Vis engineers prior to providing services for Hip implant alignment for Image based Hip planning in CORI.\n\n\n\nIdentified need for engineers’ training to prepare the engineers to respond to surgeons who may request components or surgical maneuvers not supported by the pre-operative planning framework. Engineers should be made familiar with the approaches a surgeon may take when planning cases that require components or maneuvers not supported by the framework and should be able to educate the surgeon on use of the available features to support their understanding of their planned surgical approach for the given patient. (i.e. DDH patients may require augments to fit the cup within their true, under-formed acetabulum, and may also require femoral shaft osteotomies or inferior translation/movement  of the femur (if displaced do to trauma) to correct leg length discrepancies).' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
