2026-07-21 22:34:21,785 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48495 (CSTEST-619): summary='Neck cut planning adjustment options' description='As a surgeon, I am able to see the pre-defined neck cut view and neck cut height based on Engineer’s plan of the neck cut once the plan is imported. Similarly, the latest neck cut plan should be reflected in the final plan summary and report. Example image -\n\n!image-20230619-155008.png|width=325,height=217!\n\nInitial neck cut plane (up to 2 planes) could be provided by Engineer’s plan or IDB. \n\nDuring Stem planning (type-size selection and placement), the neck cut plane(s) are also visible. When stem moves, the neck cut plane moves with it. Alternatively, surgeon could move the neck cut plane(s), translate/rotate, independent of the stem position. \n\n3D bone model should reflect the neck cut for rendering display and impingement analysis.\n\nWhen desired, surgeon can view the Neck cut Height (distance between predefined landmarks, i.e. lesser trochanter, and the neck cut plane and bone intersection landmark) otherwise the height value can be hidden during stem planning.\n\n!image-20230511-160401.png|width=518,height=531!\n\nBlue lines in the image below showing two cut planes. Red line showing a single cut plane.\n\n!image-20230619-124857.png|width=8.333333333333332%!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,786 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48496 (CSTEST-618): summary='CT slices integrated with Web Planner for implant planning' description='{color:#ff5630}*Not being considered for initial version*{color}\n\n\n\n\n\nFor user to move implant positions, 3D bone model information alone may be insufficient. In that scenario, user would want additional information to gain confidence in the new implant positions. These additional information could be CT data and hence need to ensure that the Web Planner is capable of viewing CT data.\n\n\n\nOnce the data is imported, *integrated CT* slices to demonstrate implant placement in CT reference frames with corresponding 3D bone model. The CT slice replaces the 2D outline of the 3D bone model in visualization.\n\n\n\nReference - [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-608|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-608|smart-link]\n\n2D Outline of Bone model - (used for Implant placement) Showing the outline of 3D bone model in a specific frame across the depth of 3D bone in respective reference plane (coronal/sagittal/transverse). Example - Using cross hair and 3 different views.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,786 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48497 (CSTEST-617): summary='ADLs2- Impingement Analysis by femur angles' description='* As a surgeon, I would want to know the rotation (Flexion/extension, Abduction/adduction, external/internal rotation) of the femur where initial impingement is detected. \n* When I select a specific activity, I can observe the femur angle values change as the motion for the selected activity of daily living progresses.\n* I can manually move any of the 3 angles. When I change the femur angle values, the 3D bone/implant models move to reflect the changes I enter. \n* My user experience should feel like live interaction and not where I have to wait to see the result. \n\n\n\nExample interaction could look like below.\n\n!image-20230511-161909.png|width=184,height=172!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,786 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48498 (CSTEST-616): summary='Ability to generate pre-op plan report which can be reviewed/referenced outside OR and in the OR' description='Web Planner should be able to generate a plan report on demand. It be commanded to generate an automatic report for the case at a pre-determined stage in the workflow through VCM or user may genera a report when desired. Multiple reports could be generated for the same case, so add date/timestamp/version for tracking.\n\nReport features - Once user validate the plan, either automatically or via dedicated use action Web planner generates report for that plan. \n\n* Web planner needs to generate a report which can be exported to Visionaire .\n* Web planner needs to generate a report which can be viewed on commonly used hardware devices for review, 6” to 70” screen for view only\n* Web planner needs to generate a report which can be printed by commonly used printers\n* Web planner needs to generate a report which can be viewed in Hip 7 viewer via USB import (DICOM compatible file, i.e., .dcm)\n\nPrint compatible report content should include information for - \n\n* Planned surgical outcome parameters\n* Pre-planned parameters\n* Details of Acetabulum Cup planning\n* Details of Femur stem planning\n* Details of Spinopelvic classification\n* Details of neck cut planning\n* Hide PHI data\n\nHip 7 compatible report may be tailored to view on CORI intraoperately. \n\nThe report should be compatible to be printed on a regular 8.5 X 11 inch printer paper. \n\nThe report should be compatible to be viewed on different screens from 6” to 70”.\n\n\n\n{color:#bf2600}Action: PDF encryption needed or not.{color}' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,787 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48499 (CSTEST-615): summary='Delete - Identification of implant and bone impingement for any specific ADL as the plan is updated' description='Same as [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-614|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-614|smart-link]\n\n\n\nWeb Planner needs to do live calculation to demonstrate the status of bone-bone and implant-implant impingement for all ADLs as implant parameters or anatomy parameters (i.e. SPM classification) are being changed. \n\n* As implant positions move or implant components are changed, calculate impingement possibilities for all ADLs in the background to notify user which ADLs have impingement\n* While impingement calculation is performed, the ADL icons turn grey (rather than red or green) to indicate that the data is being calculated\n* Use pre-calculations for impingement predictions to the extent it is possible to avoid delay in live calculations' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,787 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48500 (CSTEST-614): summary='ADLs1 - Simulation for Activities of Daily living (Skeleton and Patient bone with implants)' description='* As a Surgeon, I would like to know if any of the ADLs will cause impingement risk for my selected implants or implant positions. As I update the implant types/size or their placement, ADLs status should update live (live desired for user experience, in worst case, re-calculate button implementation) with new implants type/size or position. For example, if the standard Anthology stem size 4 was causing impingement, when the standard stem is changed to high offset, if the impingement is resolved the 3D bone model and ADL status icon immediately updates the status to non-impingement. \n\nAdditional details - \n\n* Web Planner needs to display the summary of ADLs impingement status all the time when implant parameters are being adjusted by the user. \n** All ADLs impingement status needs to change live with changes in implant parameters. \n** Areas of impingement are also highlighted all the time on 3D bone model and changes live with changes in implant parameters.\n* The arrangement/placement of the ADLs status needs to be approach specific - Direct Anterior/Posterior Lateral and ability to view all options\n* User is allowed to select any ADLs to view the Motion and impingement details. When a specific ADL is selected, for example Gold Swing, - Simulation of activity/motion (Golf swing) is represented on generic skeleton as well as replicated with patient specific bone model with implant placements. \n** Areas of impingement are highlighted for the user to view.\n** ROM values where impingement occurs are also highlighted. \n* User is allowed to select any of the available ADLs to view the simulation (ROM/Impingement) - Tennis, Golf swing, Yoga, etc,. An individual ADL icon will convey the information of when it is selected/not selected.\n* Web Planner needs to have a predefined set of Femur angles which surgeon can quickly run-through. Ideally, pre-sets are calculated live similar to ADLs. \n\nReferences for additional ADL features -\n\n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-617|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-617|smart-link]\n\n* [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-651|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-651|smart-link]\n\n\n\n\n\nExample concept as defined below - \n\n!image-20230511-171451.png|width=1452,height=717!\n\n!image-20230511-170355.png|width=1410,height=747!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,787 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48501 (CSTEST-613): summary='IDB harmonization between multiple platforms - Volt, Web portal, (Hip 7?)' description='Web planner will need access to implant surface files/coordinates for display and measurements. Theses files need to match with files being used by Visionaire (VOLT). This feature will identify the process and workflow of managing IDB. Exact list of implants will be determined with further input from Marketing. As default, implant currently supported by RI. Hip modeler needs to be available in the IDB.\n\nDetermine as part of the risk reduction if it needs to match with Hip 7 IDB as well. We are most likely to use the same IDB database for applicable implants (currently used by Hip 7) but need to do this exercise to understand the impact when we decide to add implants which are currently not part of the original database.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,788 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48179 (CSTEST-612): summary='Duplicate tools on same Port in Trackermap.cfg lead to incorrect tracking data' description='[https://gitlab.com/smithandnephew/robotics/Libraries/Tracking/libTrackerAPI/-/blame/0e143684f0bb13d26a90bf02b85e697304e612c5/lib/TAPITracker.cpp?page=2#L1868-1903|https://gitlab.com/smithandnephew/robotics/Libraries/Tracking/libTrackerAPI/-/blame/0e143684f0bb13d26a90bf02b85e697304e612c5/lib/TAPITracker.cpp?page=2#L1868-1903]\n\nJason Cipriani reported (before he left):\n\n_this "gutting" (from 13 years ago), which i just noticed, caught_ [~accountid:622fb5cb442e0e0069ec3440]  _& i off-guard a while back, and it really needs to be ungutted and then tested in production._\n\n_your comment (_[~accountid:5cae259d3318e72736efe8c6] _\'s) reads:_\n\n\n\n{noformat}It seems to be\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0meant to do consistency checking, but the "vpTargets" variable\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0is local, filled, then discarded with no consequence.{noformat}\n\n_but it isn\'t "with no consequence". it throws an exception if the consistency checks fail. that\'s the consequence._\n\n_the entire library is designed around the invariant that no two active trackers share port/vport number but differ in geometry file specifications, and that\'s what that checks._\n\n_without it, a misconfigured trackermap will lead to undetectable tracking errors. if "0 femur 012345.ini" and "0 tibia abcdef.ini" are in the file and are both active, that block of code you gutted causes initialization failure. without it, both are allowed to be activated, but internally they\'ll end up confused with eachother with no consequence except silently incorrect reported positions._\n\n_best case the application crashes; worst case you proceed with ambiguity as to which tracker’s data is being reported._\n\n\n\nThe work to be done for this is to re-enable the “Gutted” code and test it, at least on Atracsys as well as test the use cases which Jason reports should result in an error to ensure they actually give an error.\n\nTesting on Aurora with multi-coil use, which is the reason the offending getAuroraNumPorts() function was added, is likely a long road to hoe, but it would be better to break Aurora functionality than to have someone struggle with erroneous trackermap settings, or even worse, introduce a bug into the product line that randomly works, then all of a sudden doesn’t.' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,788 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48180 (CSTEST-611): summary='RI.INSIGHTS - add links back and forth between RI.INSIGHTS to Hip and Knee Planner tools' description='' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,788 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48502 (CSTEST-610): summary='Measurements display for reference' description='Web planner needs to match the definition of measurements with VOLT so they represent same values in VOLT plan and Web plan. All the calculations are performed for the operating leg. Leg length/offset is also calculated for the non-operating leg. The measurements needs to be calculated based on the landmarks provided by VOLT plan and implants. \n\nConsider following examples - \n\n# Spinopelvic classification/ (tilt?) - (No live measurements, only display) - Only measured on VOLT but web planner displays it and allows the user to override/change it. ADL impingement status and respective implant measurements will change accordingly to match the change.\n## SPM Classification - Allowed to override\n## Standing Pelvic Tilt - Allowed to override\n# Cup anteversion and inclination - Web planner displays the information as pet VOLT plan and allows users to change it. ADL impingement status and respective implant measurements will change accordingly to match the change.\n# Stem anteversion/retroversion rotations - Web planner displays the information as pet VOLT plan and allows users to change it. ADL impingement status and respective implant measurements will change accordingly to match the change.\n# Leg length and offset - Resultant of the change in cup and stem types/placements. Computed and displayed. Compared with native and opposite leg.\n# COR shifts - Resultant of the change in cup/stem positions. Computed and displayed. Compared against native and opposite leg. \n# Combined version - Addition of the cup and stem version values. Computed/displayed. \n# Neck cut height - Distance between two landmarks. landmark 1 may be provided by VOLT. Landmark 2 will be determined based on the neck cut plane (intersection of medial one and cut plane). Compute/display.\n# Medial wall distance - distance between cup apex and medial acetabulum wall. Compute and display.\n# Cup overhang - Cup edge from anterior acetabulum rim point. Compute and display.\n\nExample-\n\n!image-20230512-131333.png|width=725,height=263!' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,789 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48503 (CSTEST-609): summary='Implant Reference system - FP and APP' description='Web planner need to support following reference systems as some surgeons would like to use one vs another.  The cup orientation values should be represented in the selected reference plane. \n\n# FP - Frontal (Coronal) Plane\n# APP - Anterior Pelvic Plane\n\nVOLT will provide the landmarks and initial definition of these planes. User on the Web planner will be allowed to select one vs another and the display of respective measurement values will change accordingly.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,789 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48504 (CSTEST-608): summary='Visualization - Bone/Implants' description='Visualization of implants and bone model will aid in implant planning in Web Planner. Figma concepts based on formative studies will drive the final arrangement of information. On a higher level following things needs to be considered - \n\n# 3D bone model - reconstructed 3D bone model from VOLT ( examples - both pelvis (x2), and femur (x2), Femur canal (operative side), Condyles (x2))\n# 3D Implant model - Imported from IDB. Mostly solid, different color for each type of component for easy differentiations\n# 3D model view options - Ability to zoom, pan, rotate 360 degrees. Some pre-defined views such as Anterior/posterior, medial/lateral, superior inferior. \n# 3D model Opacity/Transparency - Default transparency for each components and ability to change transparency in the range of complete opaque to complete transparent.\n# 2D representation of 3D models (used for Implant placement) - Showing the cross-section/outline of 3D models in a specific frame across the depth of 3D models in respective reference plane (coronal/sagittal/transverse). Model can be scrolled to pre-defined slice thickness to view a specific slice. Any landmarks, for example COR are projected through out the slides.\n# 2D model view options - Allow user to zoom, pan.\n# 2D Xray view - Option to show Xray or DRR if provided by Visionaire Engineer’s plan only for visualization, no processing.\n# Ability to expand/shrink screen sizes during implant planning.\n\n\n\nConsider compatibility with devices to accommodates commonly used screen sizes and resolution. \n\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported browsers - Latest versions by Dec 2023 - Chrome, Edge, Safari, firefox{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported screes for interaction - tablet, laptop, desktop ==> ~10”, 14”, 24” screens{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported screens only for display ~ 32”, 50” 70”{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported view - Landscape{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported user interfaces ==> touch screen, laptop touchpad + keys, mouse + keyboard{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Supported resolution - Fine as described SOW (1920x1080, 1440x900, 1366x768, 768×1024){color}\n\n{color:#ff5630}For no-compatible or non-supported situations – {color}{color:#ff5630}*Warning*{color}{color:#ff5630} about it but let user use the app at risk. It is acceptable to have non-optimal interaction or visual for non supported situations. {color}\n\nExample-\n\n!image-20230619-153653.png|width=1643,height=859!\n\nMore example screens attached.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,789 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48505 (CSTEST-607): summary='User Profile and Credentialing- Surgeon/Tech' description="{color:#ff5630}*Only consider the authentication on Web Planner based on authentication on VCM portal.*{color}\n\nOnce user already logs in VCM portal, Web planner authenticates user without asking to log in again. \n\n\n\n{color:#ff5630}*Most likely the front end will be implemented by Visionaire portal.*{color}\n\nUser will only have to go through login/authentication process once per session for accessing the portal/plan.\n\nMost likely, the front interface will be implemented on an existing Visionaire platform hence the web planner will not have any login/credentialing interface page for the user. However, in the background, Web portal needs to ensure that only authorized users on Visionaire platform are allowed the access of Web portal. \n\nWeb Portal also needs to implement safe timeout/log out. The details associated with this function will be determined after risk assessment.\n\n\n\nDetermine the types of users who will get access to the web portal and level of privileges. Likely users of the Web portal are - Surgeon, SN Rep, SN Visionaire Engineer.\n\n\n\nFollowing functions are likely to be available on Visionaire portal. Mentioned only for reference here -\n\nAbility for the user to view currently scheduled cases.\n\nAbility for the user to rearrange cases as pert the scheduled date, patient's first name and last name, etc..  \n\nAbility for the user to view archived or canceled cases and rearrange them\n\nUsers - Surgeons, Scheduler, SN Rep" issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,790 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48506 (CSTEST-606): summary='Communication-Import/Export with VCM Cloud' description='This feature describes the underline communication and import/export capability of the Web planner between different systems/databases.\n\nConsider encryption/decryption based on compliance needs.\n\n\n\n2 copies of plan in VCM cloud- \n\n* Copy 1  - VOLT version of the plan\n* Copy 2 - Start with VOLT copy, and override with surgeon changes\n\n\n\nFor each case - Web planner needs to import appropriate parameters from their respective locations (Microsoft 360 Dynamics/ Cumulous/ Visionaire) as defined in ICD.\n\n* Surface files - Patient bone/ generic bone, implants  - Visuals and measurements (could be .bj, .stl, or .wrl files)\n* Coordinates - Pelvic coordinates, Femur coordinates, reference planes APP/Functional, respective implant to bone coordinates, femur antitorsion, combined version\n* Measurements - Measurements calculated by VOLT engineer - SPM classification, Pelvic tilt, femur antitorsion, combined version, leg length/offset\n* Meta data - patient info, surgeon info, implant parameters, etc.\n* Images - Some specific images provided by VOLT plan\n* {color:#ff5630}Xray/DRR - If Xray (DRR) provide by Volt Plan{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Notes - Any notes from Engineer/Surgeon{color}\n\nFor each case Web planner needs to export appropriate parameters to their respective locations (Microsoft 360 Dynamics/ Cumulous/ Visionaire) as defined in ICD.\n\n* Surface files - Patient bone/ generic bone, implants  - Visuals and measurements\n* Coordinates - Pelvic coordinates, Femur coordinates, reference planes APP/Functional, respective implant to bone coordinates, \n* Measurements - Measurements values - SPM classification, Pelvic tilt, femur antitorsion, combined version, leg length/offset\n* Meta data - patient info, surgeon info, implant parameters, etc.\n* Images - Some specific images as part of the workflow or upon surgeon request\n* {color:#ff5630}Notes - Any notes from Engineer/Surgeon{color}\n* {color:#ff5630}Xray/DRR - If Xray (DRR) provide by Volt Plan{color}\n* Report files - files such as finalized plan reports in formats which can be either printed or visualized in CORI Hip 7 - i.e. DICOM viewer compatible \n\n\n\nIdentify appropriate database locations for the category of data and define detailed data flow to and from various system components as part of ICD definition. \n\nDefine data types for each category after discussion with development team. \n\n\n\nInitial Data flow diagram - \n\n!image-20230511-182027.png|width=1243,height=974!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,790 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48507 (CSTEST-605): summary='Delete - Duplicate of CORI-604 Implant Size (Cup/Stem*/Liner/Head*) selection options' description='' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,790 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48508 (CSTEST-604): summary='Implant and Size Selection (Family/Cup/Stem*/Liner/Head*) options' description='The final list of implant types, size, and compatibility will be driven by the configuration of the IDB. Example implants list is below -\n\n*·\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 From the RI HIP Modeler/LifeMOD set:*\n\no\xa0\xa0 R3 cups (NO HOLE, MULTI HOLE, THREE HOLE)\u200b\n\no\xa0\xa0 R3 liners (0 deg, 20 deg, 0 deg +4, 20 deg +4, anteverted, constrained)\u200b\n\no\xa0\xa0 OR3O\u200b\n\no\xa0\xa0 Anthology\u200b + High offset\n\no\xa0\xa0 Synergy\u200b + High offset\n\no\xa0\xa0 Polarstem\u200b\n\no\xa0\xa0 Heads (CoCR, Ox, +Ceramic)\n\n*·\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0 From Hip 7.1 set:*\n\no\xa0\xa0 Redapt liners: redapt 0 deg, redapt anteverted\n\no\xa0\xa0 Redapt porous cup\n\no\xa0\xa0 Redapt mod cup\n\no\xa0\xa0 CPCS stem\n\no\xa0\xa0 Redapt stem\n\no\xa0\xa0 Spectron stem\n\n~~~~~~~*~~~~~~~~~~*~~~~~\n\n\n\n*Examples for implant selection -*\n\n!image-20230614-191803.png|width=384,height=318!\n\nExample of RI Hip Modeler implants and compatibility\n\n!image-20230619-154925.png|width=423,height=246!' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,790 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48509 (CSTEST-603): summary='Implant (Cup/Stem/Liner) Placement (Rotation/translation) options' description='Web planner allows the user to change position of the implant. Any limitations on the total allowable movement will be determined based on surgical technique or risk assessment. \n\nFeatures to consider positioning flexibility - \n\n|Cup translation - Move cup superior/inferior, medial/lateral, anterior/posterior WRT the pelvis\nAllow 0.25 mm increments/decrements\nCoronal plane - medial/lateral and superior/inferior changes\nTransverse plane - medial/lateral and anterior/posterior changes\nSagittal plane - anterior/posterior and superior/inferior changes|\n|Cup orientation - Rotate cup to change inclination or anteversion WRT the pelvis in both Frontal Pelvic Plane and Anterior Pelvic Plane\nAllow 0.5 degree increments/decrements\nRotation in each plane - Coronal, Axial, Sagittal|\n|Liner orientation (only for Lipped liner) - Rotate liner WRT cup normal axis - Allow 30 degree increments/decrements rotational changes by O’clock position (0-11)|\n|Stem position - Move stem superior/inferior, medial/lateral, anterior/posterior WRT the femur (stem?)\nAllow 0.25 mm increments/decrements\nCoronal plane - medial/lateral and superior/inferior changes\nTransverse plane - medial/lateral and anterior/posterior changes\nSagittal plane - anterior/posterior and superior/inferior changes|\n|Stem orientation - Rotate stem to change angle WRT to femur- anteversion/retroversion, varus/valgus, anterior/posterior tilt\nAllow 0.5 degrees increments/decrements \nRotation in each plane - Coronal, Axial, Sagittal|\n\nView and interaction - Example of 2D cross-section view below. Where user can place the implant in selected plane (coronal/sagittal/transverse) of reference and scroll through the slices to check it’s position w.r.t. bone. Placement arrows help in aligning position and angle. If placement arrows engaged constantly (i.e. Pressed, the movement of implant accelerates). Native and updated COR is always projected in the selected 2D slice.\n\nAbility to expand and shrink the implant plan windows. Ability to zoom pan implant plan (bone/implant).\n\nAny change in the implant position should reflect appropriate changes in the surgical outcome calculations, such as leg length and offset changes, combined anteversion changes, impingement status changes in ADLs.\n\n*Example concept of Cup and Stem placement on a Coronal plane with 2D slices of the 3D models -*\n\n!image-20230614-192629.png|width=388,height=462!\n\n!image-20230614-192606.png|width=264,height=330!' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,797 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48510 (CSTEST-602): summary='Delete  - Case Management' description="{color:#ff5630}*Don’t consider for now.*{color}\n\n{color:#ff5630}*Only consider it if the case management is implemented separately or redundant to Visionaire’s - VCM case management.*{color}\n\nAbility for the user to view currently scheduled cases.\n\nAbility for the user to rearrange cases as pert the scheduled date, patient's first name and last name.  \n\nAbility for the user to view archived or canceled cases and rearrange them\n\n\n\nUsers - Surgeons, Scheduler, SN Rep" issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,798 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48181 (CSTEST-601): summary='Pre-Op Hip Licensing Model' description='Able to follow KPOP structure?… KPOP licensing tied to NSYNC, but HPOP will not have interface with NSYNC from start.\n\n\n\n Typical things to consider - \n\nEvaluate and Confirm scope of Hip Licensing. Are we using Visionaire license? A separate Hip item or combined in any way?\n\nWill license management be linked to VCM/CRM in any way? \n\n\n\nDefinition still pending for the impact to Hip:\n\n* Discussed 06/05/2023: Ability to populate a list of Users, and their selected facilities (selected and assigned to user in NSYNC, by the user), in the VCM. Will need to pull list from NSYNC to populate list in VCM. This can be a manual process in short-term. Eventually, will move to Bridge and Bridge will support licensing. Cumulus/NSYNC can generate the list, but Visionaire will need to cross-check list with onboarded facilities/surgeons. \n** If this manual process is followed, how often will the NSYNC list need to be generated and cross-checked…. Bi-weekly suggested. Alternatively, a Visionaire user can be given access to Cumulus/NSYNC screen to check, but how often would they need to check, and would this be too labor intensive?' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,799 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48182 (CSTEST-600): summary='Pre-Op Hip - Surgeon Planning Portal' description='Overview - The Web Planner displays information of the Engineered Plan created by Visionaire Engineer. Moreover, Web Planner allows surgeon to update the plan by changing implants, or adjusting implants position to achieve desired outcome. Once agreeing to the original/updated plan, surgeon can generate report which can be used intraoperatively by either printing or importing it in CORI Hip7 application.  \n\n*Features-*\n\n# Review Engineered Plan\n# Change implants\n# Update implants positions\n# Review ADLs - summary vs specific activity\n# Review Impingements - bone-bone & implant-implant impingements, summary vs specific activity\n#  Allows free ROM input to review impingements \n# Export final plan in form of reports\n# Reports - can be printed and can be digitally viewed in the OR\n# Reports - contain summary of the plan and additional details and images of bone/dicom ct/' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,799 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48183 (CSTEST-599): summary='Pre-Op Hip - Volt and ADLs/Simulation Application' description='Develop preoperative planner for THA to fit within the Visionaire workflow for use by Visionaire engineers. Planner will be developed as a plugin called VOLTHip within LifeMOD software. Workflow steps required are: \n\n# Import Case \u200b\n# X-ray Measurements:  Spinopelvic lateral x-rays for landmarking and categorization\u200b\n# Preop Measurements:  CT scan+solid bones. Get initial pre-op measures.\xa0\u200b\n# Templating\u200b\n## Cup and Liner templating\u200b\n## Stem and Head templating\u200b\n# Postop Measurements: Capture and visualize changes to alignment\u200b\n# Impingement Analysis: RI Hip Modeler kinematics and 3D impingement\u200b\n# \xa0Case Export: Any necessary data for Web Planner.\n# Hip Implant Database setup and management: Critical piece that needs defined and accessible for both this and the Web Planner\n\n\n\nProgress is tracked on the LifeModeler board in the Hip 3D epic: [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/LIF/boards/92/backlog?selectedEpic=LIF-1148|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/LIF/boards/92/backlog?selectedEpic=LIF-1148|smart-link]' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,800 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48184 (CSTEST-597): summary='Pre-Op Hip - Visionaire Surgeon Onboarding' description='Visionaire offers surgeon-preference driven pre-operative planning solutions. In order to generate pre-operative plans which account for surgeon preferences, Visionaire must meet with each ordering surgeon to capture information regarding their surgical preferences. This activity is considered surgeon onboarding. At the time of surgeon onboarding, surgeons are also asked to provide their imaging center’s information (some may use multiple); the imaging center(s) must be on file with Visionaire.\n\n\n\nScope:\n\nPreference Sheet\n\nDatabase Update to support additional fields captured in CORI-621\n\nQualification of Image Centers\n\nProtocol Development captured in CORI-555' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,800 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48185 (CSTEST-596): summary='RI.INSIGHTS - providing the user (surgeon or staff) the ability to create a patient record in RI.INSIGHTS' description='In the Case List tab, a Plus sign could be added that would allow the user to create a new patient.  PROMs could be added for this patient.  Above/below the comments section should also include a place to upload pre-op plans, images or PDFs.' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
