2026-07-21 22:34:21,801 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48189 (CSTEST-590): summary='write the Tibia Atlas Weights to the log, or better' description='NavioShared/States/Navio_State_FemurFreeCollection.cpp’s onExit() method will write the solution to the atlas registration (weights and transform) to the NAVIO.log file.  \n\nThere is no shared Tibia free collection state, but in NavioUKR_State_TibiaFreeCollection.cpp, the onExit() method does many things similarly to the femur version, except it doesn’t include the block of code that writes the data to the log.\n\nIDEALLY, these data would be written to the CaseData (the intraop folder) like they are in TKA.  But at the very least can we please capture these in the log?' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,802 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48190 (CSTEST-587): summary='Improved Hip Center UI' description='The Confluence page below describes work toward a better Hip Center UI which has received overwhelmingly positive response from Marketing team members as well as a select surgeon group (Jan 2023 RI.Knee Summit review).\n[https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PI/pages/2834268174/RTI+Project+Make+Hip+Center+easier|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/PI/pages/2834268174/RTI+Project+Make+Hip+Center+easier|smart-link] \n\nThis page includes algorithm description, pointers to code and repositories, validation results, and a demo video.  \n\n\n\nUser comments during the Summit meeting were:\n\n\n\n“It’s easier to use”\n“We want this on the system”\n“A+”\n“Much nicer”\n“You can just go back and forth”\n“This new approach is better than Mako.. The current one is worse.”\n“That’s super. When do I get that?”' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,802 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48191 (CSTEST-586): summary='Reference File - Digital Delivery' description='--Need a method to distribute reference files to users\n\n--Version Controlled single database collecting all reference files that would be updated as needed\n\n--Process for identifying need for reference file request and subsequent update to version-controlled database\n\nLink to Reference Files Design Specification Document: [https://smithandnephew.sharepoint.com/:w:/r/sites/ri.OS2022/_layouts/15/doc2.aspx?sourcedoc=%7B61C60979-AC0A-4D19-9C19-A26CF2C40C6B%7D&file=10076785_CORI%20Reference%20Files%20Design%20Spec.docx&action=default&mobileredirect=true&clickparams=eyJBcHBOYW1lIjoiVGVhbXMtRGVza3RvcCIsIkFwcFZlcnNpb24iOiIyNy8yMzAxMDUwNTYwMCIsIkhhc0ZlZGVyYXRlZFVzZXIiOmZhbHNlfQ%3D%3D&cid=4385a691-98f7-4519-93f5-64130e099096|https://smithandnephew.sharepoint.com/:w:/r/sites/ri.OS2022/_layouts/15/doc2.aspx?sourcedoc=%7B61C60979-AC0A-4D19-9C19-A26CF2C40C6B%7D&file=10076785_CORI%20Reference%20Files%20Design%20Spec.docx&action=default&mobileredirect=true&clickparams=eyJBcHBOYW1lIjoiVGVhbXMtRGVza3RvcCIsIkFwcFZlcnNpb24iOiIyNy8yMzAxMDUwNTYwMCIsIkhhc0ZlZGVyYXRlZFVzZXIiOmZhbHNlfQ%3D%3D&cid=4385a691-98f7-4519-93f5-64130e099096|smart-link]' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
