2026-07-21 22:34:21,822 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48227 (CSTEST-547): summary='Add More Directionality Guidance to TKA Visualize Cut State' description='Surgeons requested additional directional guidance in the TKA Visualization state for Navigating the position of cut blocks. \n\nIn the Cut Visualization state the system gives feedback regarding the position of a tracked plane relative to the position of the planned TKA cut planes.  It can be used for verifying the goodness of saw cuts or navigating manual cutting instruments into the planned cut plane position.  \n\nThe system does this by displaying a purple planned cut line (static), and a live orange cut plane line that moves as the tracked tool move.   When the two lines are displayed as coincident the position of the plate probe matches the planned cut (that’s the goal).  \n\nThe system also shows angular and rotational difference between the plate probe and the planned cut via constantly updated values.  The values are display to the nearest tenth millimeter/degree and are unsigned.  \n\nThe issue is that when the difference between plate probe and planned cut is only fractions of a mm or degree it’s difficult for surgeons to know which direction they need to move the plate to achieve the plan.  \n\n!image-20220927-162450.png|width=255,height=215!' issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
