2026-07-21 22:34:21,831 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48233 (CSTEST-541): summary='Option to Show Cut Gaps in Planning' description="User's trained in manual instrumentation do not gap balance the way Cori illustrates the process.  Instead of making cuts, putting trial components in and then balancing the ligaments, manual instrumentation takes a more stepped approach.   With manual instrumentation the surgeon makes the tibia and femur distal cut, uses spacer blocks to measure the balance in extension and flexion in terms of thickness of spacer block, tweaks the femur rotation, then makes the rest of the cuts.\n\nCompetitive systems have UI which better illustrates the manual instrumentation process.  Cori needs similar flexibility in UI." issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
