2026-07-21 22:34:21,831 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48235 (CSTEST-539): summary='HW: Integrate NGFW with CORI' description='Cybersecurity assessment concluded that a security appliance is needed for CORI connectivity. Direct connection to the CORI console exposes network vulnerabilities and additional hardware is needed to protect against unwanted traffic and mitigate risk.\n\n§Next Generation Firewalls (NGFW) use static and dynamic packet filtering and VPN support to ensure connections between the network, internet, and firewall are valid and secure.\n\n§NGFWs can filter packets based on applications, allowing extensive control and visibility through analysis and signature matching.\n\n§Implementation of signature-based IPS to distinguish between safe and unwanted applications, which are then identified using SSL decryption.\n\n§NGFW features antivirus, antispam, and antimalware.\n\n§NGFW are equipped to address Advanced Persistent Threats (APTs)\n\n§Additional capabilities include Deep Packet Inspection (DPI), sandbox integration, SSL Inspection, and SSH Control.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
