2026-07-21 22:34:21,833 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48242 (CSTEST-531): summary='CORI Core Dumps Retention Period' description='Core dumps on CORI currently have a retention period of 3 days with a maximum file size of 2GB. This retention period is insufficient as it often does not give the S+N representative enough time to return to the system to export the system logs.\n\nThe RTI, Marketing, and Complaints teams have recommended changing this to *30 days* and maintaining the *2GB file size limitation*. If the system has reached the 2GB limit for core dump storage and the system crashes again, the oldest core dumps should be automatically deleted to make room for the new one.' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
