2026-07-21 22:34:21,848 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48517 (CSTEST-492): summary='UKR - Ingestion and storage of unprocessed UKR export files (Cumulus 2.0)' description='In looking to support all of S+N’s robotics-assisted indications , Cumulus must have the ability to upload, identify, and store UKR case data.\n\nThe Cumulus data upload service will need to support:\n\n* Upload of UKR case data from all CORI software versions that have been commercially available and in-use in the field\n* Identification of a case upload as UKR in File Upload list\n\nThe goal is to simply provide secure cloud storage for UKR data in the near term so that we can begin to accumulate this data as soon as possible, even if we have not yet built the ability to parse and present it.\n\nNot in scope: Parsing of UKR data for storage in Cumulus database; presentation of UKR data within the UI.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,848 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48267 (CSTEST-486): summary='Currently, it is not possible to associate a SurgeonId with a UKR case based upon the data within the case folder.   Having this identifier will be critical to developing surgeon-driven applications.' description='Being able to group cases by surgeon is important when examining case data.  The UKR case folder does not currently include a surgeon identifier.  I am asking that a surgeon identifier be added to the case data.  We are already doing ML/AI studies without the benefit of Cumulus, so I am recommending that the inclusion of a surgeon identifier not be tied to changes made to support ingesting UKR data (although the surgeon identifier should certainly be included for Cumulus).\n\nThis can be accomplished as in TKA where a file containing the surgeonId is written to the intraop folder labeled NTKR_SurgeonID.str.  Alternatively, it could be written to the NAVIO.log file in the logs folder.  The criteria are simply that the information must be contained in the case folder, so that it is available whenever the case is exported from the CORI system.' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,849 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48518 (CSTEST-485): summary='Connected CORI: Connectivity Data Egress' description='This tickets captures the business case and development effort to create an endpoint within Cumulus that interfaces with the CORI gateway device for automated upload of procedure export data via internet connection. \n\nConnect the CORI Platform to the cloud to enable better end-to-end care, reduce maintenance cost, and provide best in class product support in a secure manner.\n\n+*CORI Data out*+\n\n* *CORI Case data*\n** Main users are the Surgeons, the RARs, analytics\n* *CORI Case Log*\n** Main users are service, complaints, support services\n\nEliminate the need for USBs when transferring data from CORI.\n\nImplement automation wherever possible.\n\nProvide a low burden for deployment and implementation in CORI’s current configuration.\n\nIntroduce a non-medical gateway device that provides a single point of connectivity to the CORI platform to enable a standardized application programming interface to the S+N ecosystem.\n\n!image-20220314-171522.png|width=391,height=439!' issueType='Feature' status='Define' parent=None
