2026-07-21 22:34:21,853 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48278 (CSTEST-467): summary='Capture Manual Femur Reference Definition - TKA' description='Currently, CORI allows users to choose between the PCA defined by the system or a manually defined rotational reference.\n\nProblem: The system does not store/capture what rotational reference was used and what the deviation from PCA was (in degrees) if the user chose to redefine their reference.\n\nThis has cascading effects on the data that is collected and interpreted through RI.INSIGHTS and the AI/COE data team. Any end users of the data are unable to quantify rotation of the femoral implant with respect to a standard/uniform reference.\n\nRequest a software change to CORI that allows the system to capture, store, and report in a case export, the original location of CORI-defined PCA and the degrees of deviation from that PCA if the reference was manually defined.' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,853 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48279 (CSTEST-466): summary='Release Refurbished Drill Tracker CI ROB10014S' description='When drill trackers are returned to complaints they need to be able to be refurbished and orderable as a service CI.  A CI needs to be created in Matrix and SAP.  Inspection criteria and processes need to be established.  Appropriate labeling updates need to be completed.\n\n+*Rationale for Importance*+\nThis will relieve inventory burden created from [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-454|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-454|smart-link]  resulting in immediate increase in CORI utilization' issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,854 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48522 (CSTEST-465): summary='ActiveArm: TKA Saw Cut Order Preference' description='Prior to beginning a procedure using the [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-457|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-457|smart-link]  the user should be able to define the desired cut order.  When the user enters bone removal each cut will appear in the order it was defined prior to beginning the case.\n\nThe cut order for a user should be able to be saved between cases so it does not need to be entered every time.  The user should also have the ability to edit their saved preference prior to a case.' issueType='Feature' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,859 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48523 (CSTEST-464): summary='Remedy Log4J security vulnerability' description='a Log4j security vulnerablity was release and we need to review and upgrade log4J in the Cumulus application.   Meg is working with security on doing an assessment across our product portfolio of the Log4J critical cybersecurity vulnerability. It’s an easily misused vulnerability for any externally-facing systems that are using versions of Apache before 2.15. Here is some more detailed information if you’re interested: https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/apache-log4j-vulnerability-cve-2021-44228/\n\nThe immediate risk for Cumulus is protected via the AWS WAF that has been implemented.   We have received the WAF configuration with Viktor(Lumino) and we do see the WAF rule blocking requests. \n\nWe still need to work through all the components of the ri.Insights (Cumulus) product and upgrade the log4J versions.   This epic will be collection of tasks that need to be implement to ensure we full upgrade log4J' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,860 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48280 (CSTEST-463): summary='FAI Nav' description='FAI is an acronym for Femoral-Acetabular Impingement and refers to an arthroscopic sports medicine procedure in which the hip joint it re-shaped with a bur to improve hip flexion and reduce pain in the hip joint.  This specific ticket describes the development of an application which will be executed with the Cori platform to treat FAI through navigated resection of the femur neck.   At a high level the FAI Nav application will include the following components:\n\n* Software application which runs on the Cori console which includes UI & computation for tool calibration, guided image registration, and navigation of a cutting instrument. \n* Independent, mobile camera cart - During the FAI procedure the camera may need moved around the OR to maintain visibility with the tracked tools.  The cart mounted camera would make this difficult as the cart also houses the Cori console with handpiece, tablet, footpedal, tensioner cables running from it to the patient. \n* Collection Probe - Mechanical component used for characterization of the physical bone, necessary for image registration.  Analogous to the Cori Point Probe.  Will need to be tracked using the Cori tracking system.  \n* Cutting Tool - Mechanical component used for shaping the patients bone.  Will likely be an existing sports-med cutting wand with a tracking frame attached.  This tool will need to be tracked using the Cori tracking system.  \n\nNot included in this ticket is the development of an FAI Planning application which is necessary the deployment of an FAI but separate from the FAI Nav applicaiton.  The FAI Plan application will be run on a personal device (e.g. laptop or tablet), will use medical imaging and user interaction as input to create a resection plan to treat the patient specific case of FAI.  The plan that is the output of the ‘FAI Plan’ application will be the primary input for ‘FAI Nav’ application.' issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
