2026-07-21 22:34:21,868 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48294 (CSTEST-443): summary='Bone Debris Reduction' description="+*Problem Statement:*+\nMultiple customers have complained about bone debris leaving the surgical field.   Surgeons have concerns about material touching the surgical lights and returning to the sterile field.  Anesthesiologist are complaining that patient bone material is landing in their area and on equipment.\n\n*+Current mitigations being used to limited success include:+* \n* Technique modifications (ie. Cut Direction (left to right to have clockwise spinning flutes force material down), cutting speed modifications, distal bur approach (example: Dr. Chris Jones from Melbourne), ask anesthesiologist to move during milling (Jackson), move lights during milling (SOG), position hand to cover the cutting areas – OK Position\n* Suction - Not effective\n* Irrigation\n* Covers: Pulse lavage tip, Face shields, additional draping between anesthesia and the surgeon\n\n*+High Level User Needs and Requirements+*\n* Reduce the amount of bone debris and liquid that leaves the sterile field while using exposure control to complete the following cuts:\n* Femur: Anterior, Anterior Chamfer/Chord, Distal, Posterior Chamfer and tibia\n* Note:  The constrained access of the posterior femur cut prevents splatter\n* Allows access to all areas of the knee\n* Nice to have: Also resolves guard slipping problem\n* Reusable instrument preferred\n* Reusable Option\n* COGS less than $100\n* Fits into existing sterilization tray\n* Disposable Option\n* COGS less than $20\n* \n\nField Reports #'s below for reference:  Duke (22), Gulf Coast (1), TriStar Centenial (1), Erlanger (1),\nCASE-2020-00022287\nCASE-2020-00027229\nCASE-2020-00028837\nCASE-2020-00028838\nCASE-2020-00028790\nCASE-2020-00028789\nCASE-2020-00028792\nCASE-2020-00028791\nCASE-2020-00028794\nCASE-2020-00028793\nCASE-2020-00028845\nCASE-2020-00028844\nCASE-2020-00028846\nCASE-2020-00028841\nCASE-2020-00028842\nCASE-2020-00028840\nCASE-2020-00028839\nCASE-2020-00028843\nCASE-2020-00030694\nCASE-2020-00035354\nCASE-2020-00034952\nCASE-2021-00039266\nCASE-2021-00039264\nCASE-2021-00042766" issueType='Epic' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,868 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48550 (CSTEST-442): summary='KenSci-Data Migration Support' description='This epic will provide the support to migrate the data from KenSci to Cumulus.  This is intended to be just reload the same cases to the Cumulus application once all the data load features are created and validate the data migration.\n\nMVP\n\n-Data files that were loaded into Kensci should be taken and loaded into Cumulus platform\n\n-Processing and manipulations on the data to be dictated by the Cumulus design\n\n-There is no request or need to mimic Kensci’s mechanism for data manipulation' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
