2026-07-21 22:34:21,876 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48554 (CSTEST-437): summary='KenSci-Global Data Aggregation' description='This epic supports the KenSci Sync up to support ensuring the Cumulus application has ability to support globalized customers where users can be supported everywhere that KenSci currently supports.\n\nThis includes ensuring we have hosting and architecture that allows users to support Global data aggregation from the cases across all supported regions where regulations allow.\n\nCreate the backend and master authorizations for access to global aggregate data [https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-461|https://smith-nephew.atlassian.net/browse/CORI-461|smart-link]' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,877 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48307 (CSTEST-436): summary='Localization of the Surgeon Portal Application' description="The web application may require translation on the application's UI to a local required language.\n\nInvestigate the technology to attain the translations. Use i18n standards to implement the technology.\n\n# Work will include identifying the strings that will require translation.\n# Translate based on the language selected on the browser\n# The functions of search, sort, and filter are also applicable for the language selected.\n# Tag each string to translate to the required languages\n# Create infrastructure to maintain the tagging for future development\n\nUsers accessing the portal from a country where the native language is not English will be entering text and characters of their native language into the site. Cumulus will need to be able to store, handle, interpret, and search based on that language’s characters." issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
