2026-07-21 22:34:21,899 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48323 (CSTEST-362): summary='Registered trials within the Robotics Workflow (+update post-op gaps with this info)' description='Support registration of trial components (femur and tibia) within the Robotics workflow. The implant teams, starting with Sync instrumentations, are generating trial components with divots to allow for registration in the Robotic workflow (divots are the dimension and shape of CORI point probe and locations and dimensions were integrated in conjunction with Robotics team). \n\nUpon registering trial components, surgeons can assess position, rotation, etc which are not set by CORI, and can prep fixation features for implants accordingly. \n\nThis registration can also be used (in conjunction with entering a poly thickness) for final gap assessment to remove dependency on baseline collection for determining post-operative gaps. This is particularly valuable for use with tensioner, as currently the baseline collection does not contain any information today with the tensioner thickness.' issueType='Epic' status='Define' parent=None
