2026-07-21 22:34:21,908 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48335 (CSTEST-349): summary='Autorotation in Bone Removal' description='Update to the bone removal screens to include functionality of autorotation based on location of handpiece. Mimics effect of free collection with with purposeful rotation. Autorotation with visual guidance to allow HCP to cut perpendicular to the cut plane, includes surgeon guidance for burring (rotation on plane). \n\nFunctionality must be implemented in such a fashion that rotation is deliberate and not jarring, as user mills bone away. Functionality should be present with option for manual rotation.' issueType='Epic' status='Funnel' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,909 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48336 (CSTEST-348): summary='Add cut selection defaults as a surgeon preference' description='In the Cori TKA application the surgeon has flexibility to choose the cutting strategy that they would like to use. options are below:\n\nFemur: Bur All, Distal Bur, Distal Cut Guide\n\nTibia: Bur All, Twin Peg\n\nIn current implementation the Cori system always defaults to bur all for both femur and tibia.  The surgeon can select to change this in the Planning stages.  \n\nMost surgeons do not swap between cutting strategies from case to case, so a surgeon that prefers to distal cut the femur would need to make this selection every case.  to improve efficiency the cut selection should be moved to the surgeon preferences screen.  As preferences can be saved, the cut selection could be made more automated & surgeon specific.' issueType='Epic' status='Define' parent=None
