2026-07-21 22:34:21,912 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48560 (CSTEST-339): summary='RKA: Data export support for RKA - for import into Data Management Platform' description='Revision Knee Application\n\nData export to align with updated export for TKA and UKR in format and process. Data needs to be able to be consumed by RI.INSIGHTS. \n\nAll current data fields exported in TKA remain applicable. \n\nAdditional data fields for reporting can include: augment selections (size and location), joint line measurements. \n\n* Added data fields have been discussed with the R+D teams and information exists in EA or with SYS ENG teams from prior discussions. \n\nPlease see MVP field for minimum fields to be exported\n\nNice to Have:\n\nImage export from procedure (realistic model and relative location of reference point(s)) to indicate location of joint line reference on either the femur or the tibia\n\n* This can also be implemented with stock image in post-processing (upload) \n* Inclusion of image to be determined based on implementation prototypes and user feedback' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,912 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48561 (CSTEST-338): summary='RKA: Bone Refinement in Registration' description='This feature describes a need to create a surface which approximates the post explant tibia bone surface. The post-explant bone surface needs to be referenced during planning and also needs to be used to create a volumentric cutting model for bone removal.\n\nThis feature is needed for addition of RKA functionality. Upon completion of point collection in free collection, the software needs to create a volumetric model that can be refined to depict the surface of the bone once the original implant is removed. This will be used during planning to visualize.\nThis has a dependency on the hardware that will be used to refine: using the CORI handpiece to refine or using the CORI pointer probe with a new refining guard.\n\nSimilar to the bone refinement stage in F/T bone removal, however, we need to have this stage prior to final planning.\n\n# Creation of a volumetric model upon collection of sufficient free collection points.\n# Potentially select tool used for refining or determine based on proximity to the bone.\n# Allow for refining using handpiece\n# Allow also for refining using the pointer probe \\[Need to connect with the HW team to get the dimensions]\n# \n\n\nRevision MVP;\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt]' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,913 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48562 (CSTEST-337): summary='RKA: Joint Line Reference' description='Revision MVP;\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/LSycnp|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/LSycnp|smart-link]' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,913 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48563 (CSTEST-336): summary='RKA: Augment Planning' description='Revision MVP; EA and Prolaborate boards detail technical implementation and state position in workflow. Once augments are selected, augment choices to be maintained if HCP goes back to planning. \n\nAugment planning should use augment implant CAD.\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/LmCqqG|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/LmCqqG|smart-link]' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,913 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48564 (CSTEST-335): summary='RKA: Workflow Selection for Revision (intraoperative workflow selection)' description='Means to enable features associated with revision knee procedure, upon installation:\n\n# Means to enable the feature set (akin to total knee features enabling)\n# Means to confirm user has purchased the feature set (additional line in code)\n# Means to install Revision Implant (LEGION RK, plus augments) via the terminal.\n\nMeans to include enabled features in case workflow for Revision Procedures:\n\n# (1) Case Creation Screen\n## Procedure: TKA\n## Implant: LEGION RK\n# Surgeon Preferences Screen\n## Joint Laxity: Collect / Skip\n## Initial Implant Planning: Yes / No\n## Femur Rotational Reference: PCA / Manually Define\n## Tibia Resection: Default / +1 /+2 / +3\n## Femur Implant Referencing : Anterior / Posterior\n## {color:#ff5630}SDIP: Yes / No – TBD how implemented (not a current selection, but may be there when RKA is launched){color}\n## Rotation Center (Femur): Medial Posterior / Knee Center\n## {color:#ff5630}Femur Cut Selection: Distal Bur / Bur all (not a current selection, but may be there when RKA is launched){color}\n## Joint Line: Femur / Tibia / Both / None\n# \n\nAll preferences are available for all procedures.Selection of LEGION RK implant drives inclusion of Bone Refinement (F/T) between initial implant planning and gap assessment. Upon leaving implant planning, system will read last implant selected, should it be LEGION RK, Augment Planning will appear.If features are enabled, all should be accessed from Other Options button (joint line, refinement, augment planning).If you change implants from TKA to RK, system will prompt user to complete bone refinement stages.\n\nRevision MVP; EA and prolaborate boards describe how surgeon is able to select and complete a procedure with the added implants and added features. EA also depicts state transitions and logic for completion of workflow. \n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Repository/Artifact.aspx?repId=99685971-6983-427d-b366-71a2193839f9&procId=\\{0DF2F9FE-2CE4-4b1f-AD7D-032121352404}|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Repository/Artifact.aspx?repId=99685971-6983-427d-b366-71a2193839f9&procId=%7B0DF2F9FE-2CE4-4b1f-AD7D-032121352404%7D]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Repository/Artifact.aspx?Auth=w4fM9d73biPACn1Y31nJea%2fIjg9%2fqn62Ua%2bA2zypNpLpsO6bl8FY2UJdLM7Sw9cW3iiXIsEvN9PzgBGKs9%2buLoP3CkXklhuQJ%2bSAx%2b0kK0KHenbGvi8ZzT%2f3AbgMjqXeQPw2ph2lkqV0Kt2N43faCZIoPl7dzBeRw87ZIHlPH3oq8PF%2bEeqGtqkQ9UkOSZ3x|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Repository/Artifact.aspx?Auth=w4fM9d73biPACn1Y31nJea%2fIjg9%2fqn62Ua%2bA2zypNpLpsO6bl8FY2UJdLM7Sw9cW3iiXIsEvN9PzgBGKs9%2buLoP3CkXklhuQJ%2bSAx%2b0kK0KHenbGvi8ZzT%2f3AbgMjqXeQPw2ph2lkqV0Kt2N43faCZIoPl7dzBeRw87ZIHlPH3oq8PF%2bEeqGtqkQ9UkOSZ3x|smart-link] \n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt]' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,914 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48565 (CSTEST-334): summary='RKA: Create Revision IDB configuration' description='Add Revision components into our IDB structure. This includes the following Femur/Tibia configurations:\n\n# LEGION RK Femur / RK (constrained) Poly / LEGION RK Tibia\n# LEGION PS Femur / PS Poly / LEGION RK Tibia  ?\n# LEGION PS Femur / PS Poly / LEGION Primary Tibia\n\nThese combinations should support what would be considered standard poly. On PS tibia we should support the PS poly.  for RK we should support the RK poly.  \n\nAll to be compatible with augments per the implant designs (i.e. LEGION RK Femur, LEGION RK Tibia and LEGION PS femur are compatible)\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/mhWan]\n\n[https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt|https://prolaborate.sncloudcontrol.com/Tvmjt]\n\nAdditional information on IDB configurations, start to WI0040 process and compatibility, among other topics, can be found in MM and meeting notes from prior sessions with team (Mike C, Dave D, Kavya, Mara)' issueType='Feature' status='Backlog.' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,914 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48566 (CSTEST-333): summary='Planning: View Preferences in Planning' description='Creating an initial plan based on previous plans or preferences created by that surgeon based on averages.\n\nDisplay preferences (preferrential plan) in planning at a button press. Values cannot be changed.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,914 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48567 (CSTEST-332): summary='Planning: Utilization of Preference in Planning as Initial Placement' description='Implementation of using information set from surgeon profile as initial starting position for implant components. \n\nUse case of reverting back to CORI plan or preferred plan needed - ability to reset F/T to either preferred plan or CORI plan\n\n* There will be a button to reset the preferred plan and a button to reset to Cori default initial plan for both femur and tibia (4 buttons total, 2 newe for preferred planning reset)\n\nThe decision to use the SDIP plan vs the Cori default initial plan will be made at the surgeon planning portal in launcher.  If there is an initial plan saved for the deformity bucket that the patient falls within then Cori will apply that, otherwise use the Cori initial default plan.  No other ‘apply SDIP’ in planning or surgeon preferences is necessary.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,914 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48344 (CSTEST-331): summary='Planning: Autopopulate Averages' description='Creating an initial plan based on previous plans or preferences created by that surgeon based on averages, \n\nPlease see attached presentation for description of prototyped flow and parameters of surgeon driven initial planning, including when and where averages are displayed and when auto-population occurs. \n\nCORI system should calculate averages based on segment of case data being analyzed and auto-populate in surgeon profile, per the attached.' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,915 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48345 (CSTEST-330): summary='Planning: Display Averages' description='Creating an initial plan based on previous plans or preferences created by that surgeon based on averages, \n\nPlease see attached presentation for description of prototyped flow and parameters of surgeon driven initial planning, including when and where averages are displayed. \n\n\n\nAverages should be generated by system without user prompt. This should occur as cases are saved/allocated to the noted buckets.' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,915 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48568 (CSTEST-329): summary='Planning: Save Multiple preferences' description='Creating an initial plan based on previous plans or preferences created by that surgeon by:\n\n* Setting preferences in Surgeon Planning screen using reference files imported to the system, and\n* Updating preferences to match implant placement done in completed TKA case (at Case Review screen)  \n\nSurgeons should be able to save implant preferences for multiple deformities - set preferences/parameters for all deformity buckets. \n\nPlease see attached PPT.\n\nTo facilitate record tracking , an automatic screenshot should be taken about these preferences, in relation to the cases. and should be saved within the surgeon files. Ideally, preferences set should be exported with relevant cases in a human readable format. \n\n**Values should be able to be manipulated to the 0.5mm or 0.5 deg – This will match Combined Planning' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,915 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48346 (CSTEST-328): summary='Ability to set/change implant rotation points in TKA' description='Surgeons want the ability to change the point around an implant rotates in planning. \n\nAdditional surgeon preferences to be included (prior to and/or within planning) to optimize any adjustments after initial placement of the implant. \n\n* +Femur coronal view+ - Surgeon can intra-operatively (in planning) select/change the point about which the varus/valgus of the implant pivots \n** i.e. knee center, distal medial, distal lateral\n* +Tibia coronal view+ - Surgeon can intra-operatively (in planning) select/change the point about which the varus/valgus of the implant pivots\n** i.e. knee center, medial plateau, lateral plateau.\n* +Femur transverse view+ - Extension of Femoral Rotation Center selection - surgeon can intra-operatively (in planning) select/change the point about which the femur implant rotates \n** i.e. knee center, posterior medial, posterior lateral\n* +Tibia sagittal view+ - surgeon can intra-operatively (in planning) select/change the point about which tibia slope is pivoted. \n** i.e. anterior point, knee center\n\nThis feature shall be available in image-free and image-based workflows. Default behavior to be defined.  \n\nTo facilitate record tracking, the selected rotation points should be logged OR an automatic screenshot should be taken upon entry and exit of this state(s) and should be saved within the surgeon files. Ideally, preferences set should be exported with relevant cases in a human readable format.' issueType='Epic' status='Review' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,916 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48569 (CSTEST-327): summary='Planning: Surgeon Profile' description='Creating an initial plan based on previous plans or preferences created by that surgeon by:\n\n* Setting preferences in Surgeon Planning screen using reference files imported to the system, and\n* Updating preferences to match implant placement done in completed TKA case (at Case Review screen) \n\nGeneration surgeon profile button from “choose case” screen. Allows HCP to set/view planning preferences for various deformities. \n\nFrom this profile, the surgeon can set his/her preferences for specific implants and deformities and can choose to implement these preferences as their initial plan.  This feature can operate independently from Connected CORI features. \n\nTo facilitate record tracking, an automatic screenshot should be taken upon entry and exit of this state, and should be saved within the surgeon files. Preferences and references set should be exported with relevant cases where used, and with system log exports in a human readable format. \n\nImporting reference files:\n\nReference files created externally (outside the CORI system) will be imported and saved in the CORI system via a USB stick. A new import button will be added to the Admin Screen in Launcher to Import, View, and Delete reference files.\n\nAll imported reference files will be available for viewing and selection in the Surgeon Profile screen. On selection of a reference file in the  Surgeon Profile screen, reference values will be displayed in a format that differentiates it from the preferences being set with arrow buttons.' issueType='Feature' status='Done' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,922 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48347 (CSTEST-326): summary='Revision Indication Addition w/ technique on existing application' description='BBT document traceability to support and claim indication expansion for Revision Knee with current CORI TKA software. \n\nClinical feedback and currently utilized technique to be captured into a surgeon-authored document detailing steps. \n\n\n\n{panel:bgColor=#deebff}\nNOTE: This does not replace clinical and market need for software features specifically for revision knee, as detailed in other epics on the Kanban board. \n{panel}' issueType='Epic' status='Done' parent=None
