2026-07-21 22:34:21,925 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48354 (CSTEST-214): summary='Improve Handpiece Disconnect Recovery Dialogs' description='The Cori 1.4.3 release introduced a recovery solution for the spurious handpiece disconnect errors that were being detected by Cori.  In the recovery one of two dialog messages is displayed based on the classification of the low level error (recoverable vs. non-recoverable).  Since Cori 1.4.3 was an expedited global release, the text in the dialogs was borrowed from existing text in the system so that UI translations were not affected.  \n\n !image-2021-05-12-16-49-31-854.png|thumbnail! \n\n !image-2021-05-12-16-50-18-978.png|thumbnail! \n\nThis feature specifies work to be completed to rewrite these dialogs to be more clear.' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,926 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48355 (CSTEST-213): summary='System Error Message - Specificity Improvement' description='Product Management\n\nHandpiece Scope - Understand how/if each HP fault can result in an actionable set of steps for our reps to minimize recovery time and field perception of fault. \n\nDialog messages should be concise and actionable with direction as to how to proceed through the case.  External references or use of training materials for error codes is not actionable in a timely manner by rep in room.\n\n__________________________\n\n^ The above does not describe the feature as requested by R+D.\n\nThis feature describes the need for more specific, technically relevant content in the system error dialogs.  E.g. in some cases (see handpiece disconnect dialog)  the user action to recovery is the same for many hardware system errors. This results in the same dialogue being shown for multiple system error messages (e.g. handpiece disconnect recovery, there are 18 different low level errors which can be handled through the recovery).  This is fine for the users in the OR, but hamstrings the complaint process because field reports are written wrt very generic dialogs that the users see.   This could be accomplished by accompanying the actionable dialogue text with a more specific error codes, which communicate to developers/complaint personnel exactly which type of error is being reported by the system.' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
