2026-07-21 22:34:21,930 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48572 (CSTEST-197): summary='libPMB does not compile on Ubuntu 20.04' description="can't find various iostream concepts.  Here's a fix:\n\n{{diff --git a/PMBMonitor.cpp b/PMBMonitor.cpp\nindex 76027f4..749db05 100644\n--- a/PMBMonitor.cpp\n+++ b/PMBMonitor.cpp\n@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@\n #include <libftdi1/ftdi.h>\n #include <stdio.h>\n #include <unistd.h>\n+#include <iostream>\n \n #define DEBUG 1}}" issueType='Technical Debt' status='Triage' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,931 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48573 (CSTEST-196): summary='libBBTMat does not compile on Ubuntu 20.04' description='Libraries/Math/libBBTMath/lib/Quaternion.hpp\ngives an error complaining about fquat (quaterions based on floats) not being defined, though dquat (quaternions based on double) is.  This is due to the fact the dquats are defined redundantly, where fquats are only defined in a "fwd.hpp" header, which is included by glm.hpp.\n\n\nHere is the change that fixes the problem:\n\n{{diff --git a/lib/Quaternion.hpp b/lib/Quaternion.hpp\nindex 68a7062..990b09d 100644\n--- a/lib/Quaternion.hpp\n+++ b/lib/Quaternion.hpp\n@@ -23,8 +23,10 @@\n  *             index, q[0] etc. q[0] = q.w, q[1] = q.x and so on\n  */\n #pragma once\n+#include <glm/glm.hpp>\n #include <glm/gtc/quaternion.hpp>\n \n+\n namespace bbt\n {\n namespace Math}}' issueType='Technical Debt' status='Triage' parent=None
