2026-07-21 22:34:21,938 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48370 (CSTEST-194): summary='Exposure Mode - HP Tracker out of View Behavior' description='Request from Dr Freeman and Ana (rep): in bone removal, when the handpiece is in exposure mode and is out of view, the drill should not spin. This will more quickly indicate to them, that there is an "issue" (tracker out of view) that needs to be addressed, rather than them wondering why the drill is spinning but not removing bone. \n\nTo them, the audible/tactile feedback of a spinning drill indicates that Dr Freeman should be able to remove bone.' issueType='Epic' status='Archive' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,939 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48574 (CSTEST-193): summary='Tablet touch stops working if unplug-replug from terminal' description='Expected Behavior:\n\n* Tablet touch is available on plugging the tablet back in after unplugging the tablet\n\nActual Behavior:\n\n* Tablet touch not working\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n# Tablet, Cori Monitor (DVI) and 3rd monitor (DP) is plugged in initially\n# Resume a knee case till bur selection\n# Enter to terminal Unplug and replug the tablet\n# Exit the terminal unplug and replug the tablet\n# Repeat steps 3-4, 5 more times \n# click on the tablet screen the touch is not working\n\nVersion of Software/Hardware Where Defect Occurred:\n\n* Software: J-20210119214657 and hip_usb-20210218-sysprep.7z\n* Hardware: Console - SN000005\n\nOther\n\n* Refer Attached logs navioboot-2021-02-23-23-36-33.zip' issueType='Anomaly' status='Triage' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,939 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48575 (CSTEST-192): summary='Bone Resection Accuracy Assessment for Japan Submission' description='The Japan regulatory team has met with the regulatory body (PMDA) to discuss the CORI submission. As part of that meeting, the CORI test reports were reviewed for adequacy for submission. PMDA determined that since a primary function of the CORI system is bone removal, that numerical analysis of bone resection accuracy is necessary. As a result, TR1700 should be updated to include a section with a detailed numerical analysis of planned bone cut vs. measured surface finish.' issueType='Task' status='Triage' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,939 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48583 (CSTEST-191): summary='Dotted Pre-op graphs are showing in Post-op Gap Assessment screen even if planned preop graphs are not collected' description="Dotted Pre-op graphs are showing in Post-op Gap Assessment screen even if planned preop graphs are not collected\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Login into TKA Application and go to Pre-op Gap Assessment.\n2. Collect Manual Gaps at only one bin say at 30 degree only and make sure that graph value is somewhere around 2-3 mm only\n3. Click on Continue.\n4. In Combined Planning screen, there won't be any Pre-op graphs (which is correct)\n5. Go to Post-op gap Assessment screen.\n6. Click on graph widget icon display at RHS.\n7. System shows dotted pre-op graphs which is incorrect as there was no Planned Pre-op gap collected." issueType='Bug' status='Review' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,940 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48576 (CSTEST-190): summary='Footpedal Disconnect During Free Collection Active State' description='If the Footpedal is disconnected during free collection, the free collection state is retained after the Footpedal is plugged back in and the the continue button is pressed. I would expect free collection to stop registering points when this is encountered. Occurs both in UKA and TKA.\n\nNot part of integration test. Ryan "got creative" during integration testing and encountered this behavior.\n\nTo replicate: collect points on bone during free collection. while collecting points disconnect footpedal. re-plugin footpedal and continue. even if footpedal is not being depressed, system will still collect points, which is odd behavior.' issueType='Anomaly' status='Triage' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,940 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48577 (CSTEST-189): summary='Overheating console test - crashes' description='Expected Behavior:\n\n* At 85 degrees: CPU overheat notification appears \n* At 90 degrees: Exits intraop\n* At 95 degrees: system shut downs\n\nActual Behavior:\n\n* System took about an hour to heat up to about 75 degrees (room was fairly cold). At around 75 degrees, the system shut down fully - to blue manual icon on front panel \n* Occurred twice \n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n\n|# Copy the folder “stress-1.0.4” from the TP1438 REVH Attachments onto a USB.\nPlug the USB into the console and press *CRTL+ALT+F2* to enter Terminal 2. Enter the following command:\ncd /home/bluebelt/usb/<usbsx1>/stress-1.0.4\nsudo make install\nWhere <usbsx1> is the partition for the USB drive.|\n|# Press \n*CTRL+ALT+F1* to return to the application. Start a UKR case and proceed to the Bone Removal state. Press *CRTL+ALT+F2* to enter Terminal 2 and enter the following command:\ncd <enter>\ntemperatureMonitor.sh|\n|# Press \n*CRTL+ALT+F3* to enter Terminal 3 and enter the following command:\nstress --cpu 4\nTape a piece of paper over the fan vents at the back of the CPU.\n*Note*: The Robotic Drill can also be run to help overheat the CPU.|\n|# Press \n*CTRL+ALT+F1* to return to the application. Wait for the CPU Overheat notification to appear.\nPress *CTRL+ALT+F2* to enter Terminal 2 and verify that the temperature reported is ≥85°C.\n\\[OSWC4355]\\[OSYC0414]|\n\n----\n\nVersion of Software/Hardware Where Defect Occurred:\n\n* Optimus software: J-20201020192735\n** Hip software: hip_usb_20201123-sysprepped\n\nOther\n\n* logs to be included' issueType='Anomaly' status='Triage' parent=None
2026-07-21 22:34:21,940 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48578 (CSTEST-188): summary='Implant size and thickness buttons are not promptly working on CORI monitor (CORI issue)' description='Implant size and thickness buttons (forward button) are not promptly working on CORI monitor\n\n* Expected Behavior:\n** Implant size and thickness buttons should increase and decrease value on single touch on CORI monitor\n* Actual Behavior:\n** Implant size and thickness buttons values increase or decrease on multiple touch on CORI monitor in implant planning stage \n* Steps to Reproduce:\n** Make sure that CORI connected with CORI monitor and Tablet\n** Install latest CORI build\n** Create UKR/TKA case\n** Proceeds to Implant Planning stage\n** Try to increase (with forward button) implant size or thickness from CORI monitor, it required multiple touch to take the effect\n** Move to Tablet monitor and try to increase implant size or thickness , it is smoothly increases or decreases implant size and thickness\n* Version of Software/Hardware Where Defect Occurred:\n** J-20201020192735\n** CORI 1.4.1.3\n* Other\n\nAttached video and logs' issueType='Anomaly' status='Triage' parent=None
