2026-07-21 22:34:21,943 - INFO - Fetched source issue 48580 (CSTEST-162): summary='CORI TKA/UKA  Add easily parseable statistics for probe and HP verification' description='looking at POS-468, it would be difficult to parse, in general, the statistics over time for any successful or failed verifications.  Currently the values for failures are there, but the success are not there, and it\'s not clear how many attempts were done, etc.\n\nSomething that is better formatted that is logged like\nHP Verification {\n  state_entry = 1  \n  attempt=2\n  Ldivot error = 0.9\n  Rdivot error = 8.5\n  Best error = 0.9\n  Best Divot = L\n  Ldivot stddev = 0.08\n  Rdivot stddev = 0.23\n}\n\nThis would allow you to look at all the logs for a particular site, for example, and see if the probe may be bent by noticing lots of failures, or perhaps higher errors than normal.\n\nWithout this sort of thing, Cumulus "analytics" will not be possible.' issueType='Story' status='Triage' parent=None
